{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts","id":1298457,"title":"Sidebar on Transgender Dynasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-21T18:55:28-07:00","id":1298457,"title":"Sidebar on Transgender Dynasts","content":"I was poking around in the new Dragonblooded backer book and noticed a sidebar on transgender dynasts and found it very interesting. The Empire can be remarkably progressive in some areas.<br /> One thing that surprised me, though, was the mention about reproduction. Yes, there are numerous weird methods on producing heirs, but there's nothing in here about, say, fully physically shifting your sex to accomplish it - nor in the section before is this listed as an option. Is that something Terrestrial magic is just incapable of accomplishing? It doesn't seem that extreme, we can already do a pretty good job with products derived from natural sources and surgery in our world, so why can't sorcery or some combination of magical plants and animals accomplish it in theirs? Shaping effects come to mind, but I can't think of any off the top of my head, least of all that they'd have access ti.<br /> <br /> Has there ever been anything in any of the Exalted books, aside from Lunars, which allows a change in gender on a permanent basis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:01:40-07:00","id":1298459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts#post1298457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was poking around in the new Dragonblooded backer book and noticed a sidebar on transgender dynasts and found it very interesting. The Empire can be remarkably progressive in some areas.<br /> One thing that surprised me, though, was the mention about reproduction. Yes, there are numerous weird methods on producing heirs, but there's nothing in here about, say, fully physically shifting your sex to accomplish it - nor in the section before is this listed as an option. Is that something Terrestrial magic is just incapable of accomplishing? It doesn't seem that extreme, we can already do a pretty good job with products derived from natural sources and surgery in our world, so why can't sorcery or some combination of magical plants and animals accomplish it in theirs? Shaping effects come to mind, but I can't think of any off the top of my head, least of all that they'd have access ti.<br /> <br /> Has there ever been anything in any of the Exalted books, aside from Lunars, which allows a change in gender on a permanent basis?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sorcerous working and a hearthstone can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:27:20-07:00","id":1298464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts#post1298457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was poking around in the new Dragonblooded backer book and noticed a sidebar on transgender dynasts and found it very interesting. The Empire can be remarkably progressive in some areas.<br /> One thing that surprised me, though, was the mention about reproduction. Yes, there are numerous weird methods on producing heirs, but there's nothing in here about, say, fully physically shifting your sex to accomplish it - nor in the section before is this listed as an option. Is that something Terrestrial magic is just incapable of accomplishing? It doesn't seem that extreme, we can already do a pretty good job with products derived from natural sources and surgery in our world, so why can't sorcery or some combination of magical plants and animals accomplish it in theirs? Shaping effects come to mind, but I can't think of any off the top of my head, least of all that they'd have access ti.<br /> <br /> Has there ever been anything in any of the Exalted books, aside from Lunars, which allows a change in gender on a permanent basis?</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have commented on this. A Terrestrial Working can be as complete as current medical science in reality. Changing utterly to \u201cwhat my physical body would be if I had received different chromosomes\u201d including a fully functional different reproductive system would be a Celestial Working. Not beyond Dragon Blooded, but difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:46:56-07:00","id":1298468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298464#post1298464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The devs have commented on this. A Terrestrial Working can be as complete as current medical science in reality. Changing utterly to \u201cwhat my physical body would be if I had received different chromosomes\u201d including a fully functional different reproductive system would be a Celestial Working. Not beyond Dragon Blooded, but difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolute bullshit and makes no sense with the current workings. At best it is an ambition three terrestrial working until they literally retcon the book when a basic hearthstone can already do it there's no way you need a celestial working for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:08:39-07:00","id":1298471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298468#post1298468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's absolute bullshit and makes no sense with the current workings. At best it is an ambition three terrestrial working until they literally retcon the book when a basic hearthstone can already do it there's no way you need a celestial working for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s your basis for correlating the scale of individual hearthstone powers to the potency open ended workings?<br /> <br /> It is much easier to complete a Working than build a Manse.<br /> <br /> The Precedent of Rawar makes clear that alternate means of reproduction are more viable that full reprouctive transition. As the core book explicitly says, the rules are not perfect simulationist, and if they contradict the setting or story somewhere, it\u2019s the rules that are inaccurate in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-21-2019, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:36:06-07:00","id":1298477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298471#post1298471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s your basis for correlating the scale of individual hearthstone powers to the potency open ended workings?<br /> <br /> It is much easier to complete a Working than build a Manse.<br /> <br /> The Precedent of Rawar makes clear that alternate means of reproduction are more viable that full reprouctive transition. As the core book explicitly says, the rules are not perfect simulationist, and if they contradict the setting or story somewhere, it\u2019s the rules that are inaccurate in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you can completely make new species at ambition three ones that can breed true. All mundane species not limited to simply animals. They just can't be magical. As well as breeding stuff that can't breed together. There is absolutely nothing about reproductive gender switch screams more difficult than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:38:46-07:00","id":1298493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298477#post1298477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you can completely make new species at ambition three ones that can breed true. All mundane species not limited to simply animals. They just can't be magical. As well as breeding stuff that can't breed together. There is absolutely nothing about reproductive gender switch screams more difficult than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare cabbage, cauliflower, broccoli, kale, Brussels sprouts, collard greens, savoy, kohlrabi, and gai lan, to their singular ancestor, from which we cultivated all of them <i>many centuries ago</i>. Virtually all the world's almonds were once lethally poisonous, and now they're so benign that we throw bits of them into candy!<br /> <br /> Yet we <i>still</i> aren't very good at providing a trans person the means to procreate in the manner aligning with their gender identity. Shit, we as a culture still aren't very good at providing a trans person <i>the right to shit in the toilet</i> aligning with their gender identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-22-2019, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:42:38-07:00","id":1298494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298493#post1298493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare cabbage, cauliflower, broccoli, kale, Brussels sprouts, collard greens, savoy, kohlrabi, and gai lan, to their singular ancestor, from which we cultivated all of them <i>many centuries ago</i>. Yet we <i>still</i> aren't very good at providing a trans person the means to procreate in the manner aligning with their gender identity. Shit, we as a culture still aren't very good at providing a trans person <i>the right to shit in the toilet</i> aligning with their gender identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't have MAGIC. There is RAW no reason why it would even be remotely celestial workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:46:24-07:00","id":1298495,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the genderswap hearthstone did not make it to 3e and hearthstones are sufficiently different in 3e that I wouldn't assume any from previous editions necessarily still exist.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably put a full on gender change Working at Terrestrial 3 and giving someone the ability to just switch their own gender whenever at Celestial 2. I could see arguments for going even lower in rating though. I mean, I could imagine a Supernatural merit that let you just change genders whenever (feels like it should be worth 2 or 3 dots based on my gut and the exact execution) and Terrestrial 2 is supposed to let you give people mutations, so....<br /> <br /> Ultimately, this is something I think you might want to discuss with your ST. The Realm finds Sorcery sufficiently distasteful that, even if gender reassessment potions were easy enough to make that the Cynis could hand them out as party favors, I don't think the vast majority of people would take them up on it, so how easy it is for a Sorcerer to swap someone's gender shouldn't impact the setting too much, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Plus, being Trans and being Gay are two different things. Not everyone is going to be comfortable with a &quot;temporary&quot; genderswap in order to have children or with the necessary ...mechanics involved, let alone the possibility of having to be the other gender potentially for years (sometimes conception is hard and presumably one of the two needs to be a woman for a year to bring the child to term). So, in those cases, a Neomah still might be the preferable option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T00:00:12-07:00","id":1298533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298468#post1298468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's absolute bullshit </div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it would be all well and good to disagree with their ruling, but maybe do it with a bit of grace and civility. It isn't 2005 anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T00:11:24-07:00","id":1298537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298533#post1298533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, it would be all well and good to disagree with their ruling, but maybe do it with a bit of grace and civility. It isn't 2005 anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just it's just a disservice to the game and options. Personally I think workings just do too much and should be limited to celestial and solar sorcery at terrestrial and celestial levels. But that's not the game rules as write. Maybe it's not completely civil but I'd rather be direct over than indirect. I'm not going to mince my words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T00:37:48-07:00","id":1298542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298464#post1298464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The devs have commented on this. A Terrestrial Working can be as complete as current medical science in reality. Changing utterly to \u201cwhat my physical body would be if I had received different chromosomes\u201d including a fully functional different reproductive system would be a Celestial Working. Not beyond Dragon Blooded, but difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does mean that dynasts that do such a working upon themselves may render themselves less able to bear children, which is definitely a concern as deebs are obsessed with having children. Personally, I think it ought to be in reach of terrestrial circle, since that can make entirely new forms of mundane life and minor supernatural abilities, which should definitely qualify.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, letting it work for terrestrial tactfully avoids one big issue that the current methods of transitioning involve, which is partial or complete sterility, which is a big no-no for dynasts whom are expected to bear children. Else you place a deeb in a situation where they cannot transition without becoming a complete pariah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T00:45:05-07:00","id":1298543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298542#post1298542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This does mean that dynasts that do such a working upon themselves may render themselves less able to bear children, which is definitely a concern as deebs are obsessed with having children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the precedent of Rawar specifically lifting the normal prohibition on Sorcerous conception of children for transgender Dynasts (as that\u2019s how the Empress and her husband Rawar [a trans man] conceived both Ragara and Mnemon - though the exact method used, be it Neomah, a Woeking where the Empress drank a potion with Rawar\u2019s blood to be impregnated, or any other possibility, is not specified)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-22-2019, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T01:10:51-07:00","id":1298545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298477#post1298477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because you can completely make new species at ambition three ones that can breed true. All mundane species not limited to simply animals. They just can't be magical. As well as breeding stuff that can't breed together. There is absolutely nothing about reproductive gender switch screams more difficult than that. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Creating anew is somewhat easier than reconstructing; even magically.</span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298542#post1298542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does mean that dynasts that do such a working upon themselves may render themselves less able to bear children, which is definitely a concern as deebs are obsessed with having children. Personally, I think it ought to be in reach of terrestrial circle, since that can make entirely new forms of mundane life and minor supernatural abilities, which should definitely qualify.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, letting it work for terrestrial tactfully avoids one big issue that the current methods of transitioning involve, which is partial or complete sterility, which is a big no-no for dynasts whom are expected to bear children. Else you place a deeb in a situation where they cannot transition without becoming a complete pariah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Workings are within reach of a Terrestrial Sorcerer; they just require more effort and are a little riskier.<br /> <br /> PS: Even if you opt for non-functional transition, there are still ways to reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T01:41:02-07:00","id":1298550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298494#post1298494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have MAGIC. There is RAW no reason why it would even be remotely celestial workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules as written are that Terrestrial workings are for what one thinks should be readily and routinely within the capabilities of Terrestrial and mortal sorcerers, and Celestial workings cover things that one thinks should only be possible to them with significant effort and dedication. The examples of each Ambition level aren't holy writ.<br /> <br /> To the extent that they're worth extrapolating from, the creation of mundane life still kind of confines that circle to more mundane solutions, which limits what it can do with a pre-existing specimen. To me, the image of fully recreating a person's body from the roots up is a more dramatic and fantastical transformation.<br /> <br /> But if going by the first line, it becomes a question of how dramatic does one want to make the subject of gender confirmation. There's an argument to the idea that it's affirmative to make it such a straightforward and casual thing as it can't be in real life, but I think there's also an argument that it kind of trivialises the issues faced by trans people, maybe even to the point of erasure. To say that, in the Scarlet Dynasty, the big Exalted community propagated through reproduction, nobody who is trans there has reason to not bear a resemblance to actual trans people... to me it kind of feels more cis affirmative. I think it's different to place that level of transformation within the realms of a higher, more rarefied magic.<br /> <br /> I'll note that trans people are among the writers of What Fire Has Wrought, and while I couldn't say if they were the ones who specifically wrote about the placement of trans people in the Scarlet Dynasty, given what is apparent about the characters of Robert Vance and Eric Minton, I doubt the book would have come through in the manner that it did if any of those writers gave a feedback suggesting that it would be preferable for magic to just trivially confirm gender.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, that's the element of it that matters more to me than whether or not the rules line up 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298537#post1298537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just it's just a disservice to the game and options.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? The option still exists, it's just a bit harder. Not even harder in a way that puts it beyond the capabilities of a player, just harder in a manner that reflects a setting preference for easier option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not the game rules as write.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules as write for sorcery are more ambiguous and determined by feel, as defined by the person who created the workings system, who is also the one that has stated the line between things akin to hormone therapy and wholesale recreation of a body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's not completely civil but I'd rather be direct over than indirect. I'm not going to mince my words.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's unfortunate, though not unexpected, that you can't see a way to be both direct and civil, and equate the latter with mincing words.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T06:19:43-07:00","id":1298573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298545#post1298545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating anew is somewhat easier than reconstructing; even magically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just... I have to say no to this. It's almost always easier to modify something than create anew.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T06:22:03-07:00","id":1298574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298550#post1298550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules as written are that Terrestrial workings are for what one thinks should be readily and routinely within the capabilities of Terrestrial and mortal sorcerers, and Celestial workings cover things that one thinks should only be possible to them with significant effort and dedication. The examples of each Ambition level aren't holy writ.<br /> <br /> To the extent that they're worth extrapolating from, the creation of mundane life still kind of confines that circle to more mundane solutions, which limits what it can do with a pre-existing specimen. To me, the image of fully recreating a person's body from the roots up is a more dramatic and fantastical transformation.<br /> <br /> But if going by the first line, it becomes a question of how dramatic does one want to make the subject of gender confirmation. There's an argument to the idea that it's affirmative to make it such a straightforward and casual thing as it can't be in real life, but I think there's also an argument that it kind of trivialises the issues faced by trans people, maybe even to the point of erasure. To say that, in the Scarlet Dynasty, the big Exalted community propagated through reproduction, nobody who is trans there has reason to not bear a resemblance to actual trans people... to me it kind of feels more cis affirmative. I think it's different to place that level of transformation within the realms of a higher, more rarefied magic.<br /> <br /> I'll note that trans people are among the writers of What Fire Has Wrought, and while I couldn't say if they were the ones who specifically wrote about the placement of trans people in the Scarlet Dynasty, given what is apparent about the characters of Robert Vance and Eric Minton, I doubt the book would have come through in the manner that it did if any of those writers gave a feedback suggesting that it would be preferable for magic to just trivially confirm gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve thought about this in the context of how difficult it would be to have a story about the difficulties of being trans in the universe of Star Trek. There they have the technology to fully change your apparent species over the course of a few hours of surgury and be completely healed with no scars by the time you\u2019re finished. In fact some surgery is so advanced even deep medical exams can barely tell anything has happened. <br /> <br /> Making your body match how you feel would be even more simple and routine than having your tonsils removed is today. It makes it a lot more difficult to show a struggle. The fact that the Federation isn\u2019t the type to descriminate in that way also makes it hard to tell that story exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T07:41:15-07:00","id":1298583,"title":"","content":"I remember a few years ago comparing my experiences with players using the knack Twin Faced Hero and the Stone of Gender Transformation.<br /> The former tended to be used for genuine exploration of transgender/gender fluidity, while the latter seemed to give male characters an excuse to put on a dress and compare boob sizes. I came to the realisation that the biggest difference between the two that was producing these different effects was cost, the stone was potentially free with the Dynast Manse background and easily passed around for laughs while dropping 11xp on &quot;sometimes I'm a man/woman/neither&quot; says something about you. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298574#post1298574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve thought about this in the context of how difficult it would be to have a story about the difficulties of being trans in the universe of Star Trek. There they have the technology to fully change your apparent species over the course of a few hours of surgury and be completely healed with no scars by the time you\u2019re finished. In fact some surgery is so advanced even deep medical exams can barely tell anything has happened.<br /> <br /> Making your body match how you feel would be even more simple and routine than having your tonsils removed is today. It makes it a lot more difficult to show a struggle. The fact that the Federation isn\u2019t the type to descriminate in that way also makes it hard to tell that story exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a DS9 episode which can be summarised as &quot;Quark has a sex change, hijinks ensue.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T08:58:09-07:00","id":1298601,"title":"","content":"Can't Terrestrial workings at ambition 3 not just create new species or fusions of them but make life wholecloth? It plays magically with life in a way that is pretty fantastical and wide ranging. <br /> <br /> What was the actual logic of the reasoning that a celestial working would be needed for a complete magically redone reproductive system? I mean DB can still do them and even do it reasonably reliably with high excellency use but I feel like its short changing terrestrial 3 workings. They can do a whole lot RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:37:42-07:00","id":1298620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298601#post1298601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't Terrestrial workings at ambition 3 not just create new species or fusions of them but make life wholecloth? It plays magically with life in a way that is pretty fantastical and wide ranging. <br /> <br /> What was the actual logic of the reasoning that a celestial working would be needed for a complete magically redone reproductive system? I mean DB can still do them and even do it reasonably reliably with high excellency use but I feel like its short changing terrestrial 3 workings. They can do a whole lot RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can even make more humans whole cloth or breed two creatures which are wholy in compatable which is my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:41:44-07:00","id":1298621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298620#post1298620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. You can even make more humans whole cloth or breed two creatures which are wholy in compatable which is my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Wow. Wondering about this. What about your own personal homunculi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:00:43-07:00","id":1298628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298621#post1298621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Wow. Wondering about this. What about your own personal homunculi?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a lot more different because it goes from modification or creation into replication. And while creating people is easy creating a replica duplicate with the intent of transfering your mind into it is much much harder. It is a solar ambition working most likely to stop most dragon-blooded from being able live forever. Unless they have the mantle of brigid. <br /> <br /> Unless you are just narassistic and want mundane copies of yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-22-2019, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:54:31-07:00","id":1298660,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial Ambition 2 workings let you give a person wings, or a rhino's hide, or an extra head.<br /> <br /> I can't see that changing their gender is more extreme than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:01:14-07:00","id":1298663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298621#post1298621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Wow. Wondering about this. What about your own personal homunculi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Screw that noise, instead sorcerously create your own family. That isn't insane hubris, it is just tailoring your life experience!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:04:24-07:00","id":1298665,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial can give you a dick. Nobody said it couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value