g any of this but you.<br /> <br /> The level of complexity is based on what you actually are trying to do.<br /> <br /> Level 2: working wings<br /> Level 3: creature with working wings that breed true (new species)<br /> Celestial: creature with working wings that breeds true that also has the mind of a functioning adult with a wealth of experiences pre made<br /> <br /> T2: working but sterile gender change<br /> T3: complete gender change on a chromosomal level<br /> Celestial: complete gender change in a chromosomal label that retains personality, memories and exaltation (if applicable)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing that indicates you need celestial workings to create a mind. Celestial workings are used to create SUPERNATURAL creatures which humans are not fullstop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:36:04-07:00","id":1298732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298723#post1298723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody is saying any of this but you.<br /> <br /> The level of complexity is based on what you actually are trying to do.<br /> <br /> Level 2: working wings<br /> Level 3: creature with working wings that breed true (new species)<br /> Celestial: creature with working wings that breeds true that also has the mind of a functioning adult with a wealth of experiences pre made<br /> <br /> T2: working but sterile gender change<br /> T3: complete gender change on a chromosomal level<br /> Celestial: complete gender change in a chromosomal label that retains personality, memories and exaltation (if applicable)</div> </div> </div> </div>Having it so that using a Terrestrial exaltation to change someone's gender is going to make their memory, personality and exaltation fall off... seems like a much bigger change. I mean, I wouldn't let someone use a Terrestrial working on a captured Solar to turn them into an amnesiac mortal with no exaltation.<br /> <br /> (I can get that working but sterile gender change is less than complete gender change.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:17:13-07:00","id":1298740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298725#post1298725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing that indicates you need celestial workings to create a mind. Celestial workings are used to create SUPERNATURAL creatures which humans are not fullstop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Then why does it require so much more effort to do this with wyld shaping technique than simply creating mortals as blank slates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:19:44-07:00","id":1298741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298740#post1298740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Then why does it require so much more effort to do this with wyld shaping technique than simply creating mortals as blank slates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because wyld shaping technique doesn't require as much work or planing or XP behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:22:27-07:00","id":1298743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298741#post1298741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because wyld shaping technique doesn't require as much work or planing or XP behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>BAHAHAHA.... Oh wait... Was that not a joke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:29:28-07:00","id":1298747,"title":"","content":"So the actual quote was in reference to whether terrestrial sorcery could replicate gender reassignment surgery and if it was more or less culturally accepted than using sorcery to make offspring. It reads: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a culturally accepted option. Terrestrial workings can do basically the equivalent of what modern hormone replacement therapies + gender-affirming surgeries can do. Celestial working can do even better. </div> </div> </div>This does have a bit of ambiguity to it, I'm a little curious what better would be in this case, but that is where it lay last time someone asked the Devs about it. (Last April for the curious.)<br /> <br /> The way I see it depending on the extent of desired changes we'd potentially just be talking multiple workings at the Terrestrial level, one for handling all the more mundane gender reassignment stuff, another to get the reproductive organs working the way they're supposed to. (Testicals produce sperm/semen, ovaries contain eggs with gametes of person and release them to reproductive lining, etc.) Celestial in this case would just be doing it all at once, maybe over a much quicker time table,maybe some additional stuff to help the person deal with any physical and psychological things that the rapid transition might cause. <br /> <br /> Also on the vetoing of whisper's idea that sorcerously altering a person's gender would default to wiping their mind clean and strip of them of their exaltation. Unless for some reason you feel the rite of Gilgul is a necessary part of gender transition it isn't screwing with an exaltation.<br /> <br /> * link to quote since I'm not sure how to do the normal quote thing with a locked thread.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1203377#post1203377\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1203377#post1203377\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1203377#post1203377\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1203377#post1203377 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:43:03-07:00","id":1298750,"title":"","content":"I think it's somewhat problematic to ever say &quot;this is a Celestial circle working but you can do the same thing by piling a few terrestrial workings together.&quot; <br /> <br /> That's just not how the workings system is set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:58:42-07:00","id":1298753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298750#post1298750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's somewhat problematic to ever say &quot;this is a Celestial circle working but you can do the same thing by piling a few terrestrial workings together.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's just not how the workings system is set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither is pretending that there's a difference between a human and tyrant lizard when it comes to what a terrestrial working can do. There's no reason you can create something objectively more terrifying with a human yet can't alter your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:04:36-07:00","id":1298754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298753#post1298753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither is pretending that there's a difference between a human and tyrant lizard when it comes to what a terrestrial working can do. There's no reason you can create something objectively more terrifying with a human yet can't alter your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? You keep throwing out these kinds of statements but you've never given any evidence to back them up. <br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea what you even mean by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:09:11-07:00","id":1298756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298754#post1298754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you talking about? You keep throwing out these kinds of statements but you've never given any evidence to back them up.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea what you even mean by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mundane species is anything that doesn't have magic. You can wholecloth create a tyrant lizard with ambition 3 terrestrial sorcery. Which is much more impressive than a human. Regardless, these are both mundane species as lunars can transform into both. They don't quantify as supernatural. The examples we have in the core about terrestrial workings are much less impressive than permanently changing your gender and to pretend otherwise is to completely disrupt the system we have in place. If you want to houserule it, fine but RAW there is nothing that stops this from happening other than your own personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:29:20-07:00","id":1298763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298756#post1298756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mundane species is anything that doesn't have magic. You can wholecloth create a tyrant lizard with ambition 3 terrestrial sorcery.Which is much more impressive than a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from the perspective of sorcery. If anything it's less impressive than creating a human as it doesn't have sentience. <br /> <br /> Dangerous to humans!= more complex than humans <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless, these are both mundane species as lunars can transform into both. They don't quantify as supernatural. The examples we have in the core about terrestrial workings are much less impressive than permanently changing your gender and to pretend otherwise is to completely disrupt the system we have in place. If you want to houserule it, fine but RAW there is nothing that stops this from happening other than your own personal opinion. </div> </div> </div>You can create a human. Absolutely. <br /> <br /> You cannot create a human who had craft 5 and knows how to make armor and weapons. You most especially can't create a human who can use sorcery and has 5 dots in it. Because that's a slippery slope paved in bullshit. <br /> <br /> Slapping wings on a person != turning a person into a new species that has wings. <br /> <br /> I would also rule that a new tyrant lizard would not have any latent abilities unlocked, nor would it instantly qualify for survival charms that stopped working when you're previous familiar died. It's a new individual, same as the human in this hypothetical. <br /> <br /> Like seriously guys, think this through. If you can create an individual with sorcery in the way your suggesting, then the lunars (who are much better at sorcery and have no sigma against it) would simply create copies of every mortal dynast with slightly altered personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:30:47-07:00","id":1298765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298763#post1298763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not from the perspective of sorcery. If anything it's less impressive than creating a human as it doesn't have sentience.<br /> <br /> Dangerous to humans!= more complex than humans<br /> <br /> You can create a human. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> You cannot create a human who had craft 5 and knows how to make armor and weapons. You most especially can't create a human who can use sorcery and has 5 dots in it. Because that's a slippery slope paved in bullshit.<br /> <br /> Slapping wings on a person != turning a person into a new species that has wings.<br /> <br /> I would also rule that a new tyrant lizard would not have any latent abilities unlocked, nor would it instantly qualify for survival charms that stopped working when you're previous familiar died. It's a new individual, same as the human in this hypothetical.<br /> <br /> Like seriously guys, think this through. If you can create an individual with sorcery in the way your suggesting, then the lunars (who are much better at sorcery and have no sigma against it) would simply create copies of every mortal dynast with slightly altered personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly haven't read the sorcery workings at all because they can do that and make them equal in power to demons of the second circle. The system you are presenting is much more reasonable than what we have but that isn't the rules as we have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:33:44-07:00","id":1298769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298765#post1298765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You clearly haven't read the sorcery workings at all because they can do that and make them equal in power to demons of the second circle. The system you are presenting is much more reasonable than what we have but that isn't the rules as we have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That's weird because I could sworn that THAT WAS AT CELESTIAL LEVEL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:35:47-07:00","id":1298771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298769#post1298769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? That's weird because I could sworn that THAT WAS AT CELESTIAL LEVEL</div> </div> </div> </div>That is. Which isn't hard for lunars to do. I don't why they'd focus on a terrestrial working when they could do a celestial one and get an imitator who can actually kill dragon blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:49:05-07:00","id":1298799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298732#post1298732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having it so that using a Terrestrial exaltation to change someone's gender is going to make their memory, personality and exaltation fall off... seems like a much bigger change. I mean, I wouldn't let someone use a Terrestrial working on a captured Solar to turn them into an amnesiac mortal with no exaltation.<br /> <br /> (I can get that working but sterile gender change is less than complete gender change.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much agree, those concerns aside, on another practical also not sure that it would be cool to offer people who want to play a trans character a choice between either being able to be fully realize their physically and retain any of their sense of self mentally. I'm not sure I'd find that experience as that welcome. Seems like if you're going to go with that route of keeping a &quot;Better than Earth 2019&quot; magical transgender therapy as a more than Tier 2 Terrestrial Working for thematic reasons, because it symbolically falls into a greater and harder level of power for you (giving no opinion here on the appropriateness of that), just jump straight to what is here the Celestial level. YMMV tho, others may think about this differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:56:06-07:00","id":1298801,"title":"","content":"Epimetheus, what's the value of these boundaries of sorcerous workings to you? What's your stake in the subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:00:12-07:00","id":1298803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298801#post1298801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epimetheus, what's the value of these boundaries of sorcerous workings to you? What's your stake in the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel that it's arbitrary as hell for no reason. A dragon blooded who wants to be their perfected self shouldn't have to deal with celestial workings when nothing of not screams that it's impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:39:51-07:00","id":1298810,"title":"","content":"In case more voices need to be heard, I totally agree with Epimetheus. Arbitrarily saying that your Exaltation falls off if you are the recipient of a Terrestrial working is absolute nonsense.<br /> <br /> That quote about Terrestrial stuff being like modern medicine and Celestial about being sci-fi medicine is cool and all, but it is certainly not in line with what is written in the book. If you add wings to yourself does your Exaltation fall off or do you lose your memories? You're remaking yourself into a person with wings, so according to some people the answer should be yes. Or are the wings simply incapable of working since you didn't Celestially alter yourself? No, that's ridiculous. The same should be said about altering your sex including chromosomes since Terrestrial-3 can specifically breed true. That's chromosomes.<br /> <br /> Since wings are the go-to, I would say that magic that remakes the human body into one that has fully functioning wings is much more drastic than magic that shapes you into what around half of humanity is already sporting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:47:38-07:00","id":1298811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298803#post1298803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just feel that it's arbitrary as hell for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what about the reasons that I described, both in terms of the rules, and the underling significance to world-building and characterisation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dragon blooded who wants to be their perfected self shouldn't have to deal with celestial workings when nothing of not screams that it's impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, that's kind of the thing with Dragon Blooded though, isn't it? That there being the least powerful means that they have to deal with more things that are not precisely fair than the Celestial Exalted do. The fact that they're a sizable community, and one in which the subject of their reproduction is a significant deal, makes the disposition of queer people more pronounced, and makes it a subject in which the limits of their magic would distinctly be represented.<br /> <br /> When it comes to fantasy worlds and marginalized people, it's a difficult balance to determine whether to err on a side that says &quot;the idealised and fantastical qualities of the setting mean that many of your real life issues are easily dealt with to the point of non-existence&quot; or &quot;magic can help cope, and society might be a good deal more accommodating, but it can still be a bit of a struggle&quot;.<br /> <br /> Clearly, the queer people who worked on the book went on the side that the most commonly available magic doesn't quite overcome that limitation for the least powerful Exalted. I can see having arguments against it, but I feel as though they should still respect the difficult position that they're in and any underlying artistic integrity.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'll also note (in the argument against it being arbitrary) that this subject is neither the only nor the first time in which Vance has suggested that some of the things encompassed by Terrestrial workings ought to require a higher level when something about their scope or specificity is increased.<br /> <br /> For instance, by a basic reading of some of the descriptions of sample Terrestrial workings, it should only be at that level that you could make a cog that would rotate indefinitely, without requiring any external power input. The potential industrial ramifications of this to the setting are quite dramatic. I'll bet that if one asked Vance what kind of sorcery should be required to imbue an object with such a property, he would place it above the Terrestrial level. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:49:09-07:00","id":1298812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298810#post1298810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arbitrarily saying that your Exaltation falls off if you are the recipient of a Terrestrial working is absolute nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody in this thread has suggested that. The developer has never said that. Don't let this be an echo chamber.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Mind, this subject is straying further and further into the topic of developer intent and meaning rather than anything we can effectively discuss amongst ourselves, so once again I feel a need to suggest that people who have queries go into the appropriate thread and ask Vance directly why he views sorcery as having this application for gender confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-22-2019, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:14:47-07:00","id":1298821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298810#post1298810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case more voices need to be heard, I totally agree with Epimetheus. Arbitrarily saying that your Exaltation falls off if you are the recipient of a Terrestrial working is absolute nonsense.<br /> <br /> That quote about Terrestrial stuff being like modern medicine and Celestial about being sci-fi medicine is cool and all, but it is certainly not in line with what is written in the book. If you add wings to yourself does your Exaltation fall off or do you lose your memories? You're remaking yourself into a person with wings, so according to some people the answer should be yes.<br /> Or are the wings simply incapable of working since you didn't Celestially alter yourself? </div> </div> </div> </div>Given that I'm the one who first suggested the idea of memory loss and/exaltation falling off, and that it was explicitly clear that this was not in reference to adding mutations to a person, I'd ask that you refrain from deliberately misrepresenting my point to make your own. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, that's ridiculous. The same should be said about altering your sex including chromosomes since Terrestrial-3 can specifically breed true. That's chromosomes.<br /> <br /> Since wings are the go-to, I would say that magic that remakes the human body into one that has fully functioning wings is much more drastic than magic that shapes you into what around half of humanity is already sporting. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm going to say this one more time since it seems hard to grasp. <br /> <br /> Mutations at T2 don't breed true. <br /> Creation of a new species at T3 breeds true but nothing indicate that you can use this to replicate an individual OR in any way apply this stage to an existing individual. <br /> <br /> Let's use the wings again. There is a fundamental difference between &quot;human individual with wings added&quot; and &quot;humanoid with wings that otherwise looks human&quot; <br /> <br /> On one hand the individual's kids have wings and the other's don't. <br /> <br /> I also believe that there's a difference between the creation of a humanoid species with wings and changing a human individual INTO a humanoid species with wings. <br /> <br /> We already have examples of magically changing a person into a different thing and they're all at the Celestial level. <br /> <br /> Importantly, EVERYBODY HERE HAS WORKING WINGS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 03-22-2019, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:43:22-07:00","id":1298825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298811#post1298811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what about the reasons that I described, both in terms of the rules, and the underling significance to world-building and characterisation?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ehh, that's kind of the thing with Dragon Blooded though, isn't it? That there being the least powerful means that they have to deal with more things that are not precisely fair than the Celestial Exalted do. The fact that they're a sizable community, and one in which the subject of their reproduction is a significant deal, makes the disposition of queer people more pronounced, and makes it a subject in which the limits of their magic would distinctly be represented.<br /> <br /> When it comes to fantasy worlds and marginalized people, it's a difficult balance to determine whether to err on a side that says &quot;the idealised and fantastical qualities of the setting mean that many of your real life issues are easily dealt with to the point of non-existence&quot; or &quot;magic can help cope, and society might be a good deal more accommodating, but it can still be a bit of a struggle&quot;.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'll also note (in the argument against it being arbitrary) that this subject is neither the only nor the first time in which Vance has suggested that some of the things encompassed by Terrestrial workings ought to require a higher level when something about their scope or specificity is increased.<br /> <br /> For instance, by a basic reading of some of the descriptions of sample Terrestrial workings, it should only be at that level that you could make a cog that would rotate indefinitely, without requiring any external power input. The potential industrial ramifications of this to the setting are quite dramatic. I'll bet that if one asked Vance what kind of sorcery should be required to imbue an object with such a property, he would place it above the Terrestrial level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he's directly contradicting the text. Which means he either needs to officially errata it or his point is just as valid as mine is. The system has set levels and you can't just say well X is harder to cast than Y despite being almost exactly the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clearly, the queer people who worked on the book went on the side that the most commonly available magic doesn't quite overcome that limitation for the least powerful Exalted. I can see having arguments against it, but I feel as though they should still respect the difficult position that they're in and any underlying artistic integrity. </div> </div> </div>Workings invalidate a lot of the old characters which could only exist in 1e which is why I'm not in favor of them at all. Then again there are situations like Ledaal Kes which I heavily feel is disrespected by 3e but that is another topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:49:23-07:00","id":1298830,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's particularly obvious from the sorcery guidelines that wings are equivalent to &quot;your transformed body will function as if you were born with it&quot; versus &quot;your transformed body will function as you hoped on the gross anatomical and hormone-producing levels, but produce either nonviable gametes or the gametes appropriate to your old physiology, requiring further assistance if you wish to reproduce&quot;. And the Precedent of Rawar, which is now canon, only makes sense in the second case. <br /> <br /> Whether that was a good idea or not, I'm pretty sure canon's stuck with it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:13:12-07:00","id":1298839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298660#post1298660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial Ambition 2 workings let you give a person wings, or a rhino's hide, or an extra head.<br /> <br /> I can't see that changing their gender is more extreme than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It arguably counts as a bunch of mutations instead of just one, in which case I\u2019d say +1 Ambition for the scale-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:16:35-07:00","id":1298842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298839#post1298839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It arguably counts as a bunch of mutations instead of just one, in which case I\u2019d say +1 Ambition for the scale-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. +1 ambition? <br /> <br /> Terrestrial, ambition 2, says 'inflict mutations on a willing subject'. <br /> <br /> They didn't say 'how many mutations'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:29:48-07:00","id":1298843,"title":"","content":"New dragonblooded backer book? Have I somehow missed them releasing The Realm or Heirs of the Shogunate?<br /> <br /> Also, tangentially connected but WFHW has a character that magically changed gender. Look up Iselsi Takora, to quote the book &quot;Her face, name, and <u>even<br /> gender</u> are new, the legacy of sorcerous alchemy she learned in the far Southeast.&quot; So magical sex changes are definitely something a dragon blooded sorcerer can pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-23-2019, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:28:26-07:00","id":1298875,"title":"","content":"Sure, but Dragonblood can do Celestial workings. They're just difficult.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that quote from Vance earlier seemed reasonable; Terrestrial workings can do the equivalent to modern ops and hormone therapy, so it won't make you fertile or completely change your appearance, whereas Celestial workings can do it perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T01:07:12-07:00","id":1298877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298825#post1298825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then he's directly contradicting the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assertion that creating a new mundane life form is equivalent to fully and dramatically recreating an existing human body does not make it so, and he is not contradicting the basic summary of Celestial circle workings of &quot;things that you think should require a significant exertion of effort for Terrestrial Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system has set levels and you can't just say well X is harder to cast than Y despite being almost exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a reading of utmost rigidity that leads to absurd conclusions about the depths to which the earliest circle of sorcery leads. The only thing that it requires to adjust is to take the rules as something looser and more fluid, not something to hold to the barest letter for the sake of making complaints on the Internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Workings invalidate a lot of the old characters which could only exist in 1e which is why I'm not in favor of them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which characters?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again there are situations like Ledaal Kes which I heavily feel is disrespected by 3e but that is another topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T02:47:00-07:00","id":1298886,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you're misreading the T3 examples anyway. It says make a new mundane species or breed an example with a minor supernatural power. That doesn't mean &quot;make a supernatural creature that breeds true&quot;, it means &quot;make a supernatural creature by breeding normal ones&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T04:29:11-07:00","id":1298907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298830#post1298830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Precedent of Rawar, which is now canon, only makes sense in the second case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> We don't actually know what Rawar's deal was, he could have been born to similar culture to the Delzhan where he chose to be a man for a rite of passage but never felt he was in the wrong body.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T04:54:51-07:00","id":1298915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298907#post1298907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really.<br /> We don't actually know what Rawar's deal was, he could have been born to similar culture to the Delzhan where he chose to be a man for a rite of passage but never felt he was in the wrong body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Rawar is straight up described as having been a transgender man. The Dereth institution is valuable to Delzhan transgender people, but at its core is still something arising from a culture where gender role and gender expression are very strongly tied together, and given a certain precedence over gender identity, a matter distinct to the portrayal of that culture's perceptions. I find it unambiguous that the description of Rawar is addressing the reader in language familiar to them, rather than with ambiguities in-character. <br /> <br /> I'll also note that gender dysphoria is not synonymous with being transgender, and some people have no pressing desire to undergo the confirmation surgery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T05:47:14-07:00","id":1298926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298915#post1298915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Rawar is straight up described as having been a transgender man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said he wasn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dereth institution is valuable to Delzhan transgender people, but at its core is still something arising from a culture where gender role and gender expression are very strongly tied together, and given a certain precedence over gender identity, a matter distinct to the portrayal of that culture's perceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Dereth who pick their gender based entirely on their career aspirations or which relatives they're closest to and would revert back to identifying as their birth sex if they indefinitely left Delzhan lands because they'll get tired of correcting people. Then there are those who'd still consider it a major part of their identity and worth the trouble to preserve. Do the cultural factors involved mean they're not considered transgender?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:02:45-07:00","id":1298929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298926#post1298926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do the cultural factors involved mean they're not considered transgender?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand, no, they would not be.<br /> <br /> Depending on how much they're doing it as an expression of a more loose personal sense of gender identity, they might be genderfluid, but changing your gender expression based on culturally ingrained ideas about what gender roles are is not equivalent to having a gender identity (defined as the deeply ingrained sense of what one's gender is) that does not conform to one's assigned at birth sex.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of Dereth are really more like transvestites, a category that I feel gets unduly left out of some of these discussions; there are people who will dress and express in a manner conforming to a particular gender, and employ the pronouns utilized for the same, who still do not identify as that gender.<br /> <br /> The matter of how it's a response to rigid gender roles also complicates the subject; I find much of the Dereth akin to historically documented instances of women in more rigidly patriarchal societies who dressed and expressed as men for the apparent sake of getting into roles otherwise denied outright to them (often the military). It's hard to effectively assess whether or not they would have been trans men, as the society makes it hard to determine the distinction between that and women who are performing or disguising as men for the sake of doing something that, today, they could have effectively done as women.<br /> <br /> These details inform the complexities and the nuances of the gender spectrum. But the thing that I derive from that spectrum for the sake of this discussion is that, within that spectrum, transgender still means a particular thing, and it's not something that would encompass all of the Dereth. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T06:56:59-07:00","id":1298939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298929#post1298929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The matter of how it's a response to rigid gender roles also complicates the subject; I find much of the Dereth akin to historically documented instances of women in more rigidly patriarchal societies who dressed and expressed as men for the apparent sake of getting into roles otherwise denied outright to them (often the military). It's hard to effectively assess whether or not they would have been trans men, as the society makes it hard to determine the distinction between that and women who are performing or disguising as men for the sake of doing something that, today, they could have effectively done as women.<br /> <br /> These details inform the complexities and the nuances of the gender spectrum. But the thing that I derive from that spectrum for the sake of this discussion is that, within that spectrum, transgender still means a particular thing, and it's not something that would encompass all of the Dereth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this, yes. You're looking at a society in which &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; are not gender identities as we understand them, but bundles of social norms and obligations. They're connected to biological sex only in that your birth sex determines which set you're saddled with by default.<br /> <br /> *Some probably are trans, expressing themselves as best they can with the imperfect tools their culture has given them.<br /> *Some are almost certainly gay, and looking for a socially acceptable way to have a Technically Heterosexual relationship with someone they otherwise couldn't.<br /> *Some are women that want to fight, or men that are gifted at &quot;feminine&quot; crafts.<br /> *A few are likely men that *don't* want to fight, but also don't want to shame their families with cowardice. &quot;Having reviewed my options re: dinosaur hunting vs. weaving, I've decided weaving is for me, thanks.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T09:40:53-07:00","id":1298976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298915#post1298915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also note that gender dysphoria is not synonymous with being transgender, and some people have no pressing desire to undergo the confirmation surgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most psychological things, gender dysphoria is a continuum. I personally find mine mild enough that I've not transitioned, given a mix of family pressures, how dissatisfying I'd find a no-surgery transition, the mix of expense and bad outcomes possible for surgical transition, and younger me's desire to avoid sterility. From my perspective, even Vance's suggested limits of Terrestrial Working level coupled with the ability to use magic for conception would have been <i>so</i> much better an option than reality gave me . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:14:56-07:00","id":1299044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298830#post1298830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's particularly obvious from the sorcery guidelines that wings are equivalent to &quot;your transformed body will function as if you were born with it&quot; versus &quot;your transformed body will function as you hoped on the gross anatomical and hormone-producing levels, but produce either nonviable gametes or the gametes appropriate to your old physiology, requiring further assistance if you wish to reproduce&quot;. And the Precedent of Rawar, which is now canon, only makes sense in the second case. <br /> <br /> Whether that was a good idea or not, I'm pretty sure canon's stuck with it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting, on the other hand, only makes sense in the second case because your not permanently adding wing mutations to the gene pool every time you cast a T2 working to buff a minion. <br /> <br /> As for Rawar, nothing there mentions what level of sorcery is required. Her redness (and every other db sorcerer), can use Celestial workings, after all, and binding a neomah would still be using sorcery to reproduce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 03-23-2019, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:04:32-07:00","id":1299067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1299044#post1299044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting, on the other hand, only makes sense in the first case because your not permanently adding wing mutations to the gene pool every time you cast a T2 working to buff a minion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to read more carefully before you respond. It's the <i>second</i> case I presented where the change doesn't result in the ability to reproduce as the new form (and thus the individual who underwent a gender-confirmation Terrestrial Working still needs to use additional magic, under the Precedent of Rawar, to reproduce). The <i>first</i> case is where the transformed body functions (including reproductively) as if you were born with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:34:18-07:00","id":1299074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1299067#post1299067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need to read more carefully before you respond. It's the <i>second</i> case I presented where the change doesn't result in the ability to reproduce as the new form (and thus the individual who underwent a gender-confirmation Terrestrial Working still needs to use additional magic, under the Precedent of Rawar, to reproduce). The <i>first</i> case is where the transformed body functions (including reproductively) as if you were born with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite right, one of the perils of reading / posting on a phone with intermittent Internet. My apologies. <br /> <br /> I've edited my original post to reflect this. <br /> <br /> I'll also point out that an example of terrestrial 3 workings includes the ability of the newly created species to breed true, which is not mentioned at the T2 level. To me this was another level of differentiation between the two levels rather than implicit in the T2 level but explicit at T3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T17:39:42-07:00","id":1308552,"title":"","content":"I really like Isator levi's arguments, but I just don't know that I'd apply them here. I tend to side on the magic can help but doesn't fix everything side of the discussion in most cases, but I think if I work it out in my mind, it boils down to: <br /> <br /> &quot;Terrestrial Circle Sorcery can change your appearance, but it can't make you capable of full reproduction.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well why not?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Because it only changes your appearance, like mundane surgery and hormones.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mundane surgery and hormones being limited the way they are, is a product of the method being used to create the change. If you're using sorcery, it doesn't actually make sense for those limitations to exist. You're not sending hormone signals to the brain and then speeding things way up - or else you'd also have to claim that terrestrial circle sorcery is less effective the older the person is, and it definitely doesn't involve using advanced surgical techniques. You are reaching into someone and manipulating the nature of their body and appearance. So the only possible reason I can think of as to why a transitioned-through-sorcery individual can't reproduce, is in order to maintain some Doylist imperative that says in order to complicate a transsexual individual's life, the sorcery has to be a Celestial level working.&quot;<br /> <br /> And at that point it starts to stretch my credulity to the breaking point. I'm fine with expressing and representing the struggles of 'the real world' in game, but not at the expense of the coherency of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T18:31:18-07:00","id":1308559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298810#post1298810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case more voices need to be heard, I totally agree with Epimetheus. Arbitrarily saying that your Exaltation falls off if you are the recipient of a Terrestrial working is absolute nonsense.<br /> <br /> That quote about Terrestrial stuff being like modern medicine and Celestial about being sci-fi medicine is cool and all, but it is certainly not in line with what is written in the book. If you add wings to yourself does your Exaltation fall off or do you lose your memories? You're remaking yourself into a person with wings, so according to some people the answer should be yes. Or are the wings simply incapable of working since you didn't Celestially alter yourself? No, that's ridiculous. The same should be said about altering your sex including chromosomes since Terrestrial-3 can specifically breed true. That's chromosomes.<br /> <br /> Since wings are the go-to, I would say that magic that remakes the human body into one that has fully functioning wings is much more drastic than magic that shapes you into what around half of humanity is already sporting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the thread\u2019s been resurrected, here\u2019s what Vance said most recently with regard to the wings comparison...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Terrestrial working can do everything that modern medical transition methods, like hormone replacement therapy and gender confirmation surgeries, can do. In my head, that seems about on the same level as giving someone wings. <br /> <br /> A Celestial working to transition occurs on a much more supernatural level - you're &quot;zooming in&quot; past the body to transform the Essence that it's made up of. It carries none of the downsides of modern medical transition, much as a supernatural power of flight conferred by a Celestial working doesn't carry the downsides of wings conferred by a Terrestrial working. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T19:25:48-07:00","id":1308571,"title":"","content":"If I had to come up with a phrasing in line with the rulings, it would be something like...<br /> <br /> Terrestrial workings operate by manipulation of the crude matter from which you're already composed. The results can be quite sophisticated, but still a bit limited by the base form being worked with, and significant modifications to the internal anatomy are tricky.<br /> <br /> Getting a result indistinguishable from if that had been how you were born requires starting from the base Essence pattern and building up. That requires being up a level.<br /> <br /> It might not be to all tastes, but I think it can be read consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T21:58:35-07:00","id":1308596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308559#post1308559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the thread\u2019s been resurrected, here\u2019s what Vance said most recently with regard to the wings comparison...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sister's the OP and she only showed me the link today. I haven't really been on these forums in ages. Sorry for the Necro : \\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:09:25-07:00","id":1308602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308559#post1308559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Terrestrial working can do everything that modern medical transition methods, like hormone replacement therapy and gender confirmation surgeries, can do. In my head, that seems about on the same level as giving someone wings.<br /> <br /> A Celestial working to transition occurs on a much more supernatural level - you're &quot;zooming in&quot; past the body to transform the Essence that it's made up of. It carries none of the downsides of modern medical transition, much as a supernatural power of flight conferred by a Celestial working doesn't carry the downsides of wings conferred by a Terrestrial working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance and I are just going to have to agree to disagree on that score. The wording is incredibly silly (all sorcery is supernatural). If you want to equate 'any' form of magic in Exalted to 'modern medicine', it would be Thaumaturgy, not Sorcery. To be blunt, if you're changing someone's bodies to the point where they have breasts, feminine bone structure - and continue to have that feminine appearance long after - it is fundamentally *no different* than just making them biologically female, with a working uterus and everything. <br /> <br /> Which brings us to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I had to come up with a phrasing in line with the rulings, it would be something like...<br /> <br /> Terrestrial workings operate by manipulation of the crude matter from which you're already composed. The results can be quite sophisticated, but still a bit limited by the base form being worked with, and significant modifications to the internal anatomy are tricky.<br /> <br /> Getting a result indistinguishable from if that had been how you were born requires starting from the base Essence pattern and building up. That requires being up a level.<br /> <br /> It might not be to all tastes, but I think it can be read consistently. </div> </div> </div>This wording still acts like the external 'just cosmetic' appearance of a person is just that - crude cosmetics. Anything 'beneath that' would have to be (or approach) the raw power of the Celestial Circle. But somehow this only extends to the act of reproduction, which all of this rather problematically places on some kind of holy pedestal, as if it weren't just a fundamental part of the body's anatomy, a process carried out so long as you have all the right parts, and fundamentally no different than shaping breasts that can produce milk.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game of demigods of incredible power. The difficulty of transition is not an appropriate hurdle for them. If it's a game about heroic mortals either learning or employing Thaumaturgy to transition, that's a completely different beast, but there is no way to have any circle of sorcery be capable of a complete transformation, while also denying the ability to reproduce, and not just come off as incredibly problematic, to say nothing of inconsistent to the themes of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:20:24-07:00","id":1308606,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial Workings can do a small sample of the following:<br /> Enchant paths, warding, create hybrids, grant mutations, create completely new forms of life.<br /> <br /> If it can create new forms of life, I don't see why it can't affect a body so that it's fully female. That's child's play by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:22:04-07:00","id":1308607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308602#post1308602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">biologically female</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand you mean well, but this is not a good way to word it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T23:48:54-07:00","id":1308618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308559#post1308559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the thread\u2019s been resurrected, here\u2019s what Vance said most recently with regard to the wings comparison...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I realize what he said. It doesn't make it any less silly.<br /> <br /> That said, I can completely understand wanting to make rules that allow for having character conflict and drama, but I feel the rules should be consistent this way. If we want Terrestrial sorcery to not be capable of fully changing a person that is changed by it, then it also shouldn't be able to create whole new life forms or drastically change someone's body (wings, fire breathing, whatever). Make that into Celestial level sorcery and it becomes consistent again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T00:18:21-07:00","id":1308619,"title":"","content":"Okay so looking at the core on Terrestrials, first creating a completely new life form is in the upper limit of emerald circle sorcerery ie the point where the line is starting to blur between that and celestial. <br /> <br /> Second, the description the book goes with ,and I'm guessing where Vance is pulling for his own opinion on the matter, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Workings of the Terrestrial Circle are generally rooted in transforming, enhancing, or weakening pre-existing elements of the natural world, rather than directly invoking supernatural forces. </div> </div> </div>Add in that the rest of the examples in the ambition box seem to go more off the idea of having base creatures available. Examples listed include crossing two species to create a hybrid with the best traits of both its progenitors, granting mutations, create a new mundane form of life, or breed in a minor supernatural trait to augment the strongest aspect of a creature. With the examples we're probably more talking about warping a rabbit into a vizzerdrix as opposed to creating a masticore from nothing more than a drawing you made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T03:46:41-07:00","id":1308631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308607#post1308607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand you mean well, but this is not a good way to word it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a transwoman myself, how would you suggest I word it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T04:23:17-07:00","id":1308636,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;granting mutations&quot; bit is probably supposed to involve like, physically grafting wings onto the subject or something. It's not just &quot;poof, you can fly now&quot;.<br /> <br /> As such, I don't think it can alter individuals on the genetic level. The upper bound is <i>breeding in </i>new traits. Think selective breeding vs genetic engineering. Terrestrial sorcery can do the former (for magic stuff) but altering someone's reproductive capabilities would involve the latter.<br /> <br /> It's not just a mechanical alteration, you're changing how a person's cells divide. That's something that occurs at the DNA level. So yes, it would require that the person be fundamentally restructured to be &quot;biologically female&quot;, as you put it. Or at least, their new uterus would need to be.<br /> <br /> You could probably do a uterus and ovary transplant, but then the kid would technically be the donor's child and that might mess up inheritance or some shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-29-2019, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:16:32-07:00","id":1308643,"title":"","content":"Having followed all of this, it seems a bit overly heated for what amounts to either nothing if it's part of your character's backstory that this was done for them, or something that's not particularly hard to pull off in-character as long as you have time.<br /> <br /> Just throwing the DB Occult Excellency at it with maxed out dice-pools, has extremely low odds of failing any individual roll (consider spending WP and stunts if you really want to be careful) and the base terminus of 5 is enough even if padding it out a bit is never a bad thing; assuming you go with a Finesse of 1 (and then it's really how much you trust your ST not to be an ass about it).<br /> <br /> Yes, it would be easier and more reliable if it was a Terrestrial working, but as few times as it's going to be done (there's only going to be so many trans DBs, and only so many of them are going to want to fully change their body with Sorcery, etc.) and the relatively low odds of failure... if you want this to be part of the story it's not some huge leap just because the devs ruled it a Celestial working. <br /> <br /> So, seriously. Putting aside all of the &quot;this is equivalent to that,&quot; debates which aren't going anywhere... is there any serious mechanical issue here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:03:33-07:00","id":1308657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308602#post1308602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This wording still acts like the external 'just cosmetic' appearance of a person is just that - crude cosmetics. Anything 'beneath that' would have to be (or approach) the raw power of the Celestial Circle. But somehow this only extends to the act of reproduction, which all of this rather problematically places on some kind of holy pedestal, as if it weren't just a fundamental part of the body's anatomy, a process carried out so long as you have all the right parts, and fundamentally no different than shaping breasts that can produce milk.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not saying that it's purely cosmetic, I'm saying that the lower circle is limited in rearranging the already existing substance and structure. My use of the term &quot;crude matter&quot; was a Star Wars reference.<br /> <br /> I intended not to limit it to the subject of reproduction by expressing in terms of internal anatomy overall. That there would be other kinds of internal structural changes that would be beyond that circle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is no way to have any circle of sorcery be capable of a complete transformation, while also denying the ability to reproduce, and not just come off as incredibly problematic, to say nothing of inconsistent to the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I suppose that Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is not capable of complete transformation. I feel as though such would be consistent with the difference between spells such as Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and Incomparable Body Arsenal.<br /> <br /> The comparison to generating life... even setting aside Eric's picture of it as being something that generates a neonate, I imagine that as a simpler process for drawing together the raw materials and setting the original spark of life in them, where an already existing being (especially at maturity) is structurally complex and delicate, reliant on a bunch of systems functioning in coordination and that have, in the course of their life, likely developed a lot of unique quirks and adaptations that can be hard to pin down precisely. It feels intuitive to me that a magic that would have to deal with the physical matter needs to be very careful interacting with that, lest it put a number of things in the wrong place and cascade failures result.<br /> <br /> I know very little about computers, but I have a vague impression that one which has been in operation for a while accumulates a lot of oddities that can be hard to find or fix, and there are times that it's easier to do something with a brand new one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T09:46:18-07:00","id":1308702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308657#post1308657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I'm not saying that it's purely cosmetic, I'm saying that the lower circle is limited in rearranging the already existing substance and structure. My use of the term &quot;crude matter&quot; was a Star Wars reference.<br /> <br /> I intended not to limit it to the subject of reproduction by expressing in terms of internal anatomy overall. That there would be other kinds of internal structural changes that would be beyond that circle.<br /> <br /> That is why I suppose that Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is not capable of complete transformation. I feel as though such would be consistent with the difference between spells such as Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and Incomparable Body Arsenal.<br /> <br /> The comparison to generating life... even setting aside Eric's picture of it as being something that generates a neonate, I imagine that as a simpler process for drawing together the raw materials and setting the original spark of life in them, where an already existing being (especially at maturity) is structurally complex and delicate, reliant on a bunch of systems functioning in coordination and that have, in the course of their life, likely developed a lot of unique quirks and adaptations that can be hard to pin down precisely. It feels intuitive to me that a magic that would have to deal with the physical matter needs to be very careful interacting with that, lest it put a number of things in the wrong place and cascade failures result.<br /> <br /> I know very little about computers, but I have a vague impression that one which has been in operation for a while accumulates a lot of oddities that can be hard to find or fix, and there are times that it's easier to do something with a brand new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understood what you were saying, I get the impression you don't understand what I was saying. It was late and it's possible I worded it badly.<br /> <br /> When it comes to sex characteristics, you don't really get to pick and choose what makes sense to be doable, and what *doesn't*. Again, the primary limitations in modern medicine stem from the method of transition themselves. When I said 'skin deep' or 'just cosmetic', I'm referring to the fact that you keep using phrases like 'internal structure', as if the internal structure of the body is some how different from restructuring fat, bone, skin, and so on. If the lower circle is limited to rearranging the already existing substance and structure - to mutations as well - then there is still no reason why you can't do a complete 'full transition'.<br /> <br /> between primary sex characteristics and secondary sex characteristics, there are analogs. It's why we use hormones to affect secondary sex characteristics at all. If you want to create a second X chromosome, that's as &quot;simple&quot; as triggering a genetic mutation. Now the transgender character has two X chromosomes, and the natural engines of reproduction will pass things down normally because it's not built on some sorcerous foundation, the process of reproduction already looks for those things - that person has them - job done.<br /> <br /> If you want to shape a clitoris and vagina, those things have direct analogs with the penis, testicles, etc. I'm not going to host a complex biology lecture on a subject I'm not exactly qualified to discuss, but you can research this stuff pretty easily. There is no way you can interpret Terrestrial Circle sorcery as 'rearranging the already existing substance' which would not also make a 100% complete transition possible. Medical science today is limited only in how well the body responds to hormone therapy, and what analogs are so closely related that you can create them using physical surgical methods. Sorcery doesn't have to rely on that, and like - again - thaumaturgy. Thaumaturgy would be the thing to use for a system which is miraculous for being able to achieve modern results with herbs and stuff, but still might come up short for women who want to carry a baby to term themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know very little about computers, but I have a vague impression that one which has been in operation for a while accumulates a lot of oddities that can be hard to find or fix, and there are times that it's easier to do something with a brand new one. </div> </div> </div>I don't know how this is supposed to be a good metaphor or analogy, really. Human bodies aren't computers, they're infinitely more flexible than a piece of hardware, and even ignoring all of that, it would still boil down to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, you then need to decide which parts of the computer aren't worth dealing with 'past birth',which things do you pick?&quot;<br /> <br /> And stating that this includes primary sexual characteristics (but just the ones used for reproduction) is kind of yikes.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: if you can make a penis and testicles into a vagina, clitoris, ovaries, etc, which are then functional (and there's no reason why they shouldn't be) then there is no reason why a transgender person who transitioned through sorcery could not be a parent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 04-29-2019, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:23:03-07:00","id":1308716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308702#post1308702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I understood what you were saying, I get the impression you don't understand what I was saying. It was late and it's possible I worded it badly.<br /> <br /> When it comes to sex characteristics, you don't really get to pick and choose what makes sense to be doable, and what *doesn't*. Again, the primary limitations in modern medicine stem from the method of transition themselves. When I said 'skin deep' or 'just cosmetic', I'm referring to the fact that you keep using phrases like 'internal structure', as if the internal structure of the body is some how different from restructuring fat, bone, skin, and so on. If the lower circle is limited to rearranging the already existing substance and structure - to mutations as well - then there is still no reason why you can't do a complete 'full transition'.</div> </div> </div> </div>If what you're saying here is true, then every time someone buffed a minion with sorcery they'd be injecting an entirely new trait into Creation's genepool. Every time you give someone wings, you'd give any more decendents they have wings as well. <br /> <br /> It's more like the difference between performing surgery and rearranging DNA of a living person. Terrestrial sorcery is doing the former, Celestial is doing the latter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308702#post1308702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">between primary sex characteristics and secondary sex characteristics, there are analogs. It's why we use hormones to affect secondary sex characteristics at all. If you want to create a second X chromosome, that's as &quot;simple&quot; as triggering a genetic mutation. Now the transgender character has two X chromosomes, and the natural engines of reproduction will pass things down normally because it's not built on some sorcerous foundation, the process of reproduction already looks for those things - that person has them - job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Creation doesn't have genetics. You'd not really changing DNA you're changing the fundamental essence makeup of a person. Earth Science does not equal Creation Science. <br /> <br /> Even if it did, that's not what adding a mutation <i>does. </i>If you give someone wings, they do not have 'wings' DNA or Creation equivalent. They just have some wings grafted on. <br /> <br /> Changing the fundamental makeup of a person is not 'just a mutation' it's a fundamental change to the person. Giving someone the ability to breathe fire is not just a mutation either. By your argument it would be<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308702#post1308702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to shape a clitoris and vagina, those things have direct analogs with the penis, testicles, etc. I'm not going to host a complex biology lecture on a subject I'm not exactly qualified to discuss, but you can research this stuff pretty easily. There is no way you can interpret Terrestrial Circle sorcery as 'rearranging the already existing substance' which would not also make a 100% complete transition possible. Medical science today is limited only in how well the body responds to hormone therapy, and what analogs are so closely related that you can create them using physical surgical methods. Sorcery doesn't have to rely on that, and like - again - thaumaturgy. Thaumaturgy would be the thing to use for a system which is miraculous for being able to achieve modern results with herbs and stuff, but still might come up short for women who want to carry a baby to term themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? <br /> <br /> Modern science can't give someone an y-chromosome when they don't have one, nor can it remove an existing y-chromosome. You can definitely replicate some things with hormone therapy, but like with any medical intervention, there can be drawbacks and side-effects. <br /> <br /> Where do you get the idea that thaumaturgy has any ability to perform transformations of any nature? Like, have you read the thaumaturgy section? It's pretty niche and explicitly less powerful than sorcery or charms. What you're suggesting is a significant divergence from that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308702#post1308702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how this is supposed to be a good metaphor or analogy, really. Human bodies aren't computers, they're infinitely more flexible than a piece of hardware, and even ignoring all of that, it would still boil down to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, you then need to decide which parts of the computer aren't worth dealing with 'past birth',which things do you pick?&quot;<br /> <br /> And stating that this includes primary sexual characteristics (but just the ones used for reproduction) is kind of yikes.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: if you can make a penis and testicles into a vagina, clitoris, ovaries, etc, which are then functional (and there's no reason why they shouldn't be) then there is no reason why a transgender person who transitioned through sorcery could not be a parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I'm sorry but, what? Where does this idea come from? Because you can perform cosmetic surgery on a person therefore you can create functioning reproductive organs of whatever gender you want doesn't make a lot of logical sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:31:36-07:00","id":1308717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1298468#post1298468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's absolute bullshit and makes no sense with the current workings. At best it is an ambition three terrestrial working until they literally retcon the book when a basic hearthstone can already do it there's no way you need a celestial working for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Absolute bullshit&quot; is a bit rough. It's arbitrary, because it can only be arbitrary. Such limitation is a good way to give terrestrial medicine-working sorcerers wondrous power, but power too costly to solve everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:45:41-07:00","id":1308720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308716#post1308716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, I'm sorry but, what? Where does this idea come from? Because you can perform cosmetic surgery on a person therefore you can create functioning reproductive organs of whatever gender you want doesn't make a lot of logical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are essentially paying the cost of a sorcerous working for cosmetics. When you can make wings that fully enable flight. That's just fucking great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:16:56-07:00","id":1308727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308720#post1308720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are essentially paying the cost of a sorcerous working for cosmetics. When you can make wings that fully enable flight. That's just fucking great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus man, calm down.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Wings mutation:<br /> Can you fly: YES<br /> Are you treated as a mutant by pretty much everyone you meet for the rest of your life: YES<br /> Can you ever disguise yourself as anything else: Pretty much NO<br /> Can you fit through doorways: NOT WELL<br /> Small spaces: NOPE<br /> <br /> Celestial level flight:<br /> Can you fly: YES<br /> Are you treated as a mutant by pretty much everyone you meet for the rest of your life: NO<br /> Can you ever disguise yourself as anything else: YES<br /> Can you fit through doorways: YES<br /> Small spaces: YES<br /> <br /> Terrestrial level gender swap:<br /> Can you have sex? YES<br /> Do people instantly identify you as your preferred gender: YES<br /> Do you get treated as a member of your preferred gender: YES<br /> Can you have kids: YES FOR FUCKS SAKE JUST TALK TO A NEOMAH, YOU'RE ALREADY A SORCERER AT THIS LEVEL IF YOU'RE COMPLAINING ABOUT XP COST<br /> <br /> Celestial level gender swap:<br /> can you have sex? YES<br /> Do people instantly identify you as your preferred gender: YES<br /> Do you get treated as a member of your preferred gender: YES<br /> Can you have kids: YES, unaided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:24:19-07:00","id":1308735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308727#post1308727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have kids: YES FOR FUCKS SAKE JUST TALK TO A NEOMAH, YOU'RE ALREADY A SORCERER AT THIS LEVEL IF YOU'RE COMPLAINING ABOUT XP COST</div> </div> </div> </div>You really don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:31:33-07:00","id":1308740,"title":"","content":"Ok.<br /> <br /> I don't get it. <br /> <br /> You can give someone marble skin. Wings. Extra limbs. <br /> <br /> But changing them from male to female is too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:35:12-07:00","id":1308742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308735#post1308735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I don't get why you consider the ability to reproduce the only thing that matters for a human being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:36:57-07:00","id":1308745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308716#post1308716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If what you're saying here is true, then every time someone buffed a minion with sorcery they'd be injecting an entirely new trait into Creation's genepool. Every time you give someone wings, you'd give any more decendents they have wings as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you really need to read any of the Lunar books, especially Glories of the Most High (Luna). I'm not arguing you create an entirely new trait, I'm arguing that the traits as they exist in humans already are analogous, you're just flipping a switch. Comparing a transition to giving someone fire-breathing is pretty silly when there are plenty of species that can transition their sexual characteristics without too much of an issue. Literally all sorcery would have to do, is enable that for humans.<br /> <br /> And how exactly does your Ars Magica Essential Nature theory play out? You're basically arguing that those things should be added without any changes having been made whatsoever. If genetics aren't 'real' in Exalted, then because of how reproduction works in Exalted, essence has to basically function the same way, or nothing makes sense anymore. So if you want to say it's a change to the person's essence, I'm 100% fine with that, doesn't change how things work, though. If anything it just makes things more problematic when you start treating sex as some Essential Feature of an organism which can't be changed, as opposed to a complex biological spectrum with lots of moving parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's more like the difference between performing surgery and rearranging DNA of a living person. Terrestrial sorcery is doing the former, Celestial is doing the latter. </div> </div> </div>If sorcery is just surgery, then terrestrial circle sorcery is not even capable of the barest of bare bone transitions. You'll still be taking estrogen supplements the rest of your life, you'll still have to perform aftercare in order to prevent complications later in life (dilating, etc). If you're a transman, you're even more out of luck if: &quot;All sorcery can manage is modern day surgical equivalent.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that Creation doesn't have genetics. You'd not really changing DNA you're changing the fundamental essence makeup of a person. Earth Science does not equal Creation Science. </div> </div> </div>See above. I'm not going to go combing the books for all the little ways First Age exalts, and Lunars in general, meddle with the genetics (or not-genetics) of a person. If genetics don't exist you just made my job easier because that's one less factor to consider. If you want to treat it as an essence-based system, then you could just as easily conceive of some kind of &quot;Ergi system&quot; wherein dressing and behaving as a woman alters the flow of essence in your body, resulting in someone &quot;Becoming a Woman&quot; over time. The toxic vikings were &quot;right&quot; <b>all along!</b> &lt;/sarcasm&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if it did, that's not what adding a mutation <i>does. </i>If you give someone wings, they do not have 'wings' DNA or Creation equivalent. They just have some wings grafted on. </div> </div> </div>Transitioning isn't adding features that weren't there. It's analogous, that means it's like flipping a switch. A switch which already held that possible function already. I'm feeling like a broken record here, but you don't seem to be getting it. They. Aren't. Comparable. I guess you're just gonna have to take my word on this, at this rate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changing the fundamental makeup of a person is not 'just a mutation' it's a fundamental change to the person. Giving someone the ability to breathe fire is not just a mutation either. By your argument it would be </div> </div> </div>Changing a single chromosome from a an X to a Y, or vice versa, is a <b>genetic mutation</b> that is capable of occurring in real life. It is not <b>an exalted mutation reflected in the mechanics</b>. <br /> <br /> Also a chromosome is not 'fundamental to a person' anymore than hair color, eye color, the size of your breasts, whether or not you have a penis, etc. If you can change one\u2014you can change the other. Broken Record. Again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Based on what? </div> </div> </div>A pretty elementary and easy to back-up knowledge of biology, as well as the development of sexual characteristics in the womb?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Modern science can't give someone an y-chromosome when they don't have one, nor can it remove an existing y-chromosome. You can definitely replicate some things with hormone therapy, but like with any medical intervention, there can be drawbacks and side-effects. </div> </div> </div>Modern science is forced to rely on appeasing the endocrine system so that the body can make changes on its own, without any additional prompting. Modern medicine is limited in its capacity for change, because at the moment it relies on hormone transmitters, and changes that can be created with a knife - those changes plus hormones result in parts that are functional and identical to the air-quotes &quot;the real thing&quot;. Doctors whose job it is to study such things have been - more air quotes - &quot;Fooled&quot; by the result. The reason is because those parts are so analogous that literally all you gotta do is take a knife and rearrange things to suit a different configuration\u2014all of the 'parts' are already there. You want proof? If you look at the bottom of your scrotum, you'll see a dark line, or 'crease', this would have been your vaginal folds if you'd developed differently in the womb, the dark line is essentially a scar where the flesh fused together. <br /> <br /> So again, not the same thing as wings, and definitely not the same thing as fire-breathing.<br /> <br /> Also you're coming pretty dang close to a: &quot;Transition is unsafe and has drawbacks! Hormone therapy should only be done as a last resort and will almost certainly give you cancer!&quot; person, and I just want to point out that if you continue down that path, and that prediction bares out, I'm just not going to engage with you. I really have no patience for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where do you get the idea that thaumaturgy has any ability to perform transformations of any nature? Like, have you read the thaumaturgy section? It's pretty niche and explicitly less powerful than sorcery or charms. What you're suggesting is a significant divergence from that. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and thaumaturgy from second edition as well. Did you miss the part where cloning bread is possible? So why on earth would it be impossible for a thaumaturgist to create a potion that mimics the effects of real world hormone therapy, while also being 'knife wise' enough to perform any surgeries? Hell, I wouldn't even have an issue with the potion performing everything we can do right here.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, their snarky little jab at not-Jesus getting beaten down in Nexus implies that other 'miracles' are possible, and that the one where you double food portions is only a 1 dot thaumaturgy ritual. You could conceivably design a rite based on the practices of the cult of Cybel, and have that produce a full and complete transition, by that logic. It might involve severing your genitalia and dumping a sacrificial bull's worth of blood on you, but based on precedent there's no reason why it couldn't reproduced with thaumatugry, even if you did design it as a 'two dot ritual'. <br /> <br /> This is just 'not' the hill to die on when it comes to what sorcery can and cannot do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OK, I'm sorry but, what? Where does this idea come from? Because you can perform cosmetic surgery on a person therefore you can create functioning reproductive organs of whatever gender you want doesn't make a lot of logical sense. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say 'in this world we can perform surgery on genitalia, so sorcery can 'create brand new sex organs!' I said: &quot;All of these parts are analogs of each other, you are not creating something from scratch. <b>You are not creating something from scratch.</b> If genetics is a lie and it's all just essence, it's even more explicitly 'just flipping a switch'. I still wouldn't go with that, because if you do, it's implied that the normal 'correct' essence of things exists in a binary, and if someone exists outside of that binary, then it's because the Wyld or Malfeas or some shadow land or whatever else, tampered with the perfection of the gods. Which plays into a pretty dark narrative. <br /> <br /> Sorcery isn't a knife. Sorcery isn't hormones. Sorcery is messing with the 'code' of existence, and if you can mess with that code to change one set of sexual organs to their analogous equivalent, then you can produce any of the other changes associated with it. Any other excuse you come up with is either going to stem from a problematic place of &quot;But that's sacred and can't be approached by lesser magic/science!&quot; or &quot;But it's really important to me that I include this conflict in the story, and I guess I just don't want to create that conflict by making sorcerers uncommon enough to be a problem, or I don't want to have said sorcerer make them jump through hoops for it, or <b>they're</b> a sorcerer and this is part of their character's path.&quot; I'm sorry, if it's the last one then it's just not coherent to the setting. Play a heroic mortal, have them seek out thaumaturgical secrets to transition, and then when faced by the shortcomings of their magic, have them persevere, that's a perfectly good backstory/origin plot for a Twilight Solar, or even a Zenith. <br /> <br /> Also, just as an aside? Transwomen can give birth using a transplanted uterus (provided they take anti-rejection drugs), they are already\u2014and have been for some time\u2014working on 'growing' a uterus using host cells that is 'biologically identical' to the recipient transwoman. So even if Terrestrial Sorcery is limited to the upper limits of what is possible with modern science - it would <b>still</b> be possible, you're just growing the parts in the person's body, instead of the way we do it, and you wouldn't have to surgically implant it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:40:27-07:00","id":1308746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308742#post1308742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I don't get why you consider the ability to reproduce the only thing that matters for a human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly are giving someone wings with terrestrial magic, and giving someone the ability to fly apropos of nothing with celestial magic, at all congruous with performing a sex change?<br /> <br /> For someone asking others to calm down, you could stand to take a few chill pills yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T13:31:19-07:00","id":1308770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308727#post1308727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you have kids: YES FOR FUCKS SAKE JUST TALK TO A NEOMAH, YOU'RE ALREADY A SORCERER AT THIS LEVEL IF YOU'RE COMPLAINING ABOUT XP COST</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you get the point if you think that's &quot;enough.&quot; Not to mention this is really demeaning in general. Jerk.<br /> <br /> This idea that Terrestrial Sorcery can only do cosmetic surgery or modern science is not really supported by the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Workings of the Celestial Circle are miracles of outright supernatural power, either rewriting the laws of the natural world on a relatively large scale or instilling supernatural power into the mundane world. They can have scope sufficient to place powerful blessings or curses upon an entire village or a particular neighborhood or feature of a city, and their power is either an overt manifestation of supernatural magic, or a dramatic and drastic change to the properties of the natural world. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing outright supernatural about reproduction, even in Exalted, and a single person's gender is massively not in the Celestial scope.<br /> <br /> Again - if you can create <i>life</i> at the Terrestrial level (and you can) then you create functional reproductive organs along with it. There is nothing that says said life can't reproduce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 04-29-2019, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T13:46:52-07:00","id":1308777,"title":"","content":"Look guys, Celestial circle power is for things like blasting fire from your eyes or throwing lightning bolts out of fingertips. <br /> <br /> Changing someone's gender, down to the reproductive level, is never going to be on that level of difficulty or significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T14:35:21-07:00","id":1308790,"title":"","content":"Except... it's not that difficult for a DB to do.<br /> <br /> Nobody's getting anywhere with this whole Terrestrial vs. Celestial level arguments. Everyone's made their cases, nobody's saying anything that's actually compelling to the other side.<br /> <br /> But the actually impact of the dev's ruling in practical play is also being ignored. If a DB can fairly reliably pull it off as a Celestial Working... how much does it really matter? Moving past whatever issues you have with the arbitrary call Vance made, does it actually stop you from doing what you want to do in play? Does it even significantly impact it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T15:16:15-07:00","id":1308803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308790#post1308790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody's getting anywhere with this whole Terrestrial vs. Celestial level arguments. Everyone's made their cases, nobody's saying anything that's actually compelling to the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you're assuming that the purpose of a debate (which is what this is, at this point) is to sway the other side, generally speaking it isn't. This is an open forum where anyone can read what we have to say, and if the person is on the fence, seeing either argument might be a deciding factor in what position they end up taking.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why does it matter to you if people agree with you or not? It's a game.&quot; Someone might say.<br /> <br /> I enjoy arguing. I feel like arguing with people in this thread lets me sharpen the arguments I have for why I feel the way I do, and scrutinize the foundation for those beliefs a bit more closely. What that means is that if I use my ideas in the future, I will have a better understanding of why I want to pursue that interpretation, and how I got there in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the actually impact of the dev's ruling in practical play is also being ignored. If a DB can fairly reliably pull it off as a Celestial Working... how much does it really matter? Moving past whatever issues you have with the arbitrary call Vance made, does it actually stop you from doing what you want to do in play? Does it even significantly impact it? </div> </div> </div>It matters to me because the basis for these decisions, including Vance's, demands that the biological features that allow for reproduction be treated as, at best, fundamentally dissimilar from any other part of a person's biology when that is not the case. At worst it sets it up as some sacred essential quality that cannot be approached with all but the most powerful of dragon-blooded sorcery - while also contradicting the themes and power levels of the game. <br /> <br /> These beliefs, which can be critical to an interpretation like: &quot;Yes terrestrial circle sorcery can transform someone's body, but it can't reproduce a naturally occurring body part the way it can with literally anything else.&quot; are capable of leaving a lasting impact in the people who just accept them as true and valid, and can have a harmful impact on how people like me are viewed and treated in society.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I've got a stake in it. I've got a stake in whether or not person's ability to reproduce is somehow 'Celestial' rather than 'Terrestrial', and when that kind of viewpoint isn't supported by the setting as a whole, I'm going to dispute that. I don't care if Vance said it or not, it does not matter if he's a writer, because Exalted as a whole is first, a collaborative enterprise, and second it's still entirely possible to criticize their design choices even if they were the <b>sole </b><b>author</b> of the entire extended property. Saying that the ability to reproduce requires Celestial level workings is bad writing, and here's why:<br /> <br /> You can just read everything I've already said, for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T15:47:56-07:00","id":1308810,"title":"","content":"As for whether or not you would need Terrestrial vs Celestial level working in order for a complete sex transformation I think your millage is going to vary based on Storyteller fiat more then anything else.<br /> <br /> Personally I think you are going to get more value by considering what type of story you want to tell through the use of a transgender characters or npcs and how the access to these forms of magic shapes how the story, rather then using some source book or another to justify your answer. After all each persons gaming table is going to have unique quirks that suit people playing. You and your group should pick the one that appeals most to the group as a whole and helps you tell the stories that you find most interesting and evocative regardless of cannon interpretations, Similarly there is little point in trying to force your personal opinion on the cannon interpretation of the point onto other groups, as there is nothing really to be gained by the argument. <br /> <br /> Here's how I would look at this particular problem<br /> As a transwoman myself, who has face some amount of adversity due to my identity, I personally identify strongly with characters that have had struggles due to their marginalized status especially members queer communities. As such I enjoy stories that allow me through my characters to overcome that adversity in a safe environment, which is one of the things I enjoy about tabletop role-playing. Settings and rules which ignore LGBT struggles by hand waving them away with easy access to magic or &quot;enlightened&quot; culture about gender don't necessarily appeal to me as it feels like they scrub away the struggles of LGBT people in a way that ignores our existence and personal experiences.<br /> <br /> However,<br /> I have also played with other members of the LGBT community in my group that have told me that their feelings are the exact opposite of mine. That role playing games are one of the ways that they escape from some of the hardships and discrimination that they have faced, and that the game serves as a meaningful method of self expression and wish fulfillment where they are able to explore what it would be like to lives as gay/trans/etc in a world that was accepting of their status, and that easy access to sorcery or other magic that could change their gender didn't give them a feeling of erasure of personal struggle, but a genuine way to explore their identity in a way they cant in reality. So when hosting games for these people I simply made changes to the setting that would make the games more enjoyable for them.<br /> <br /> I think that both of these ways of looking at the problem are valid, but will be preferred by different people, but the goal should ultimately be to maximize the enjoyment of your table.<br /> However at the point where we are arguing over the reproductive capabilities of transgender people in regards to sorcery order to win an internet argument about what the so called canonical state of a games magic system, rather then discussing how we can use the setting in way that that can improve the enjoyment and engagement of our players. I wont call it offensive but it does seem to be in a bit of poor taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23987-chellgame","name":"Chellgame","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T15:59:34-07:00","id":1308811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308803#post1308803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an open forum where anyone can read what we have to say, and if the person is on the fence, seeing either argument might be a deciding factor in what position they end up taking.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. What new point has been made in the past 5 pages for those readers? Watching you guys circle around making the same exact points at each other over and over certainly hasn't helped me decide how I feel about it. I see the merits of both sides, but since everyone is just arguing past each other (meaning it's not really a debate, debates involve actually engaging with the other side's points and trying to make a case that incorporates their point of view; not just both sides saying they're right with different words again) I remain as uncertain as to how I want to handle things now as I have since page 1.<br /> <br /> That's why I moved to asking about the practical impact this has on actually playing the game. As a fence sitter, making a case that the dev's ruling is a significant negative impact on play is something that would help me get off the fence for my own games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone might say. </div> </div> </div>I didn't, so please don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It matters to me because the basis for these decisions, including Vance's, demands that the biological features that allow for reproduction be treated as, at best, fundamentally dissimilar from any other part of a person's biology when that is not the case. </div> </div> </div>That's not addressing the question. If you want to hone your argumentation, don't dodge so you can restate your stronger point instead of addressing what was said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At worst it sets it up as some sacred essential quality that cannot be approached with all but the most powerful of dragon-blooded sorcery - while also contradicting the themes and power levels of the game. </div> </div> </div>Solar Ambition 3 Workings are the only thing explicitly off-limits to DB sorcerers. So this isn't the case. Mechanically this is something I can make a starting level DB that can do reliably. If this is the worst it does? It's not really bad as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These beliefs, which can be critical to an interpretation like: &quot;Yes terrestrial circle sorcery can transform someone's body, but it can't reproduce a naturally occurring body part the way it can with literally anything else.&quot; are capable of leaving a lasting impact in the people who just accept them as true and valid, and can have a harmful impact on how people like me are viewed and treated in society. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate this aspect of your position, but we're ultimately debating how hard it is for Sorcery to accomplish something, not if it can or can't. In the Exalted setting, sorcerers can totally give a trans person the body they want as fully as they want. This is why I bring up that doing it as Vance ruled doesn't really impede this happening. The harm seems minimal at worst if it basically comes down to, &quot;DB sorcerers take more time to do it, but can still totally do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, I've got a stake in it. </div> </div> </div>Nobody denied this is the case?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:32:29-07:00","id":1308820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308631#post1308631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a transwoman myself, how would you suggest I word it?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Designated female at birth.&quot; It's the same number of syllables as &quot;biologically female,&quot; even.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I'm not trans myself. But when one of my trans friends corrected <i>me</i> about this, I listened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T17:21:33-07:00","id":1308833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308770#post1308770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you get the point if you think that's &quot;enough.&quot; Not to mention this is really demeaning in general. Jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Watch it with the personal attacks. </b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T20:37:14-07:00","id":1308872,"title":"","content":"Without a massively-detailed system of mathematically-rigorous magical &quot;physics&quot; for Creation, far beyond not only the scope of the game but beyond the ability of the writers to actually create, it is literally impossible to say definitively what level of working &quot;should&quot; be able to accomplish what level of transformation. All people can do is argue by analogy, and argue which analogies are more relevant, and it's pointless because there's no underlying reality to point at to test the &quot;should&quot;.<br /> <br /> With no available underlying reality, what magic can do at what level is instead dictated by &quot;story&quot;. And we know the story here is one where the Precedent of Rawar is important, meaning that transgender Dynasts actually need there to be a social precedent for using sorcery to reproduce because their marriages are otherwise going to be barren.<br /> <br /> Now, it is perfectly fair to believe <i>that story sucks</i>. <br /> <br /> But in the context of that story, there are two possible reasons I can see for such a precedent being needed. The first is that gender-affirmation sorcery is not regularly used by transgender Dynasts. The second is that the kind of gender-affirmation sorcery regularly used by transgender Dynasts is not complete enough to make them able to reproduce without further sorcerous intervention.<br /> <br /> The first is defensible; there could quite plausibly be a social taboo against using sorcery for gender-confimation so strong that few transgender Dynasts ever undergo it. It would have to be a pretty severe one, though.<br /> <br /> The second also has a patina of plausibility. For example, ovaries, testes, and adrenal glands all make testosterone, and all make estrogen, but only ovaries make ova while only testes make spermatozoa. So magically tweaking the ratio of those hormones produced by someone's gonads (or removing them while tweaking their adrenal glands to start producing more of the desired hormone) can look like a smaller change than transforming them into their counterpart. It's not iron-clad logic from the descriptions of workings that the difference is Terrestrial-versus-Celestial instead of the difference between levels of Ambition or Finesse within Terrestrial workings, but there is plausibly a difference.<br /> <br /> So, which explanation feels like the &quot;better&quot; one for canon given the existing &quot;Transgender Dynasts&quot; boxed text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T20:57:16-07:00","id":1308878,"title":"","content":"I would also like to bring up the ever fun fact that majority of, well Creation actually, find sorcerers a combination of unnerving, weird, creepy, dangerous, and suspicious.* So many would probably also be unwilling on the grounds that you are trusting a person who your family likely only fails to label as a crazy person due to being able to make this stuff work perform massive and near complete restructuring of your physical form. Like just from the time thing, maybe you get a maybe plant that produces fruit/berries that will slowly alter your physical form so long as you have 2 cups a day and the changes should be done in a month or two. Or maybe you get it quick because the working causes you to just get parts of yourself broken down and rebuilt in sequence by swarms unidentified fleshy bugs.<br /> <br /> This is not counting what might happen if the sorcerer wants to be helpful, because I can think of a number of complaints I've heard about the female anatomy over the year (menstrual cramps and periods being the big number) that I could see a person trying to help a friend not deal with if they were going for a more idealized form.<br /> <br /> <br /> *And that's likely just if you're related to one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T04:05:45-07:00","id":1308907,"title":"","content":"As a transitioned transwoman and lesbian myself I have to back up Chellgame.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wish the struggles of the real world present in my games, and that can include anything, from class struggle to sexism or racism, and yes, sometimes also lbgt issues. And other times I would not, or just a selection of them. In short, that means that I dial up or down certain aspects of the setting anyway, though preferably not by whitewashing or cheapening real life issues. Usually just not putting the focus on them is sufficient. <br /> <br /> But lets move on the question at hand: whether a magic down-to-the-very-core transition, complete with reproductive capabilities is terrestrial or celestial does make some difference in how it plays out in the setting: namely who can afford it.<br /> <br /> The poor are out of luck. Retaining the services of a Sorcerer for about a month to two months, depending on how much finesse you can afford and his skill, which I assume also requires your own presence, so not working during that time, that sounds like it is usually reserved for the very wealthy.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to add neomah-less reproduction we're talking about retaining the services of a Terrestrial Sorcerer for probably more than half a year, and a Dragonblooded one (or better) is highly advised if you want to both minimize unfortunate side-effects due to low finesse or even outright failure. Best option will be a Celestial level Sorcerer of course. Yeah, this is solely for the hyper-wealthy.<br /> <br /> Ok, now for dialing up or down this only becomes a question you need to answer when either a player decides to play a transgender character who has a clear wish to transition, or an npc struggling with this very desire is introduced. ST and player want this to be a meaningful struggle I could imagine bumping both of the above up a few steps as in most games start with one of the pc's having the necessary money or even more likely, someone will have Terrestrial circle sorcery. Finding a few weeks of downtime is hardly a struggle. If making it trivial is the desired option on the other hand, well, as demonstrated, that is the default for most campaigns. TLDR, let this be dictated by the needs of the story.<br /> <br /> But much more importantly: discussions about whether conferring a reproductive system are Terrestrial or Celestial should really be spun off to another thread.<br /> <br /> Let's <i>please </i>avoid conflating gender and the capacity or willingness to have children (or even a period). It is not unique to transgenders, so, for a variety of reasons which I'll avoid going into, it's perhaps better to not have it in a thread with transgender in the title? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T04:26:36-07:00","id":1308908,"title":"","content":"Losing battle, Angwe. This type of topic brings forth questions that are way too hard to answer for this forum's zeitgeist to ever allow answering.Some of those are actually hard questions too. The only way to not have this type of conflation brought up is to not talk about it at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T05:27:57-07:00","id":1308913,"title":"","content":"Also, that's basically what this thread is about. <br /> <br /> Literally, that's the main issue raised in the OP. &quot;Ok, so terrestrial can get you most of the way, but why can't it let you reproduce?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T06:23:34-07:00","id":1308915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308913#post1308913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that's basically what this thread is about.<br /> <br /> Literally, that's the main issue raised in the OP. &quot;Ok, so terrestrial can get you most of the way, but why can't it let you reproduce?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware, but finish the first part of that question: most of the way where? Being a man or woman? You see wherein the problem lies?<br /> <br /> Just wish to say that reproduction has <i>nothing</i> to do gender, with or without the trans prefix, and by extension, transitioning, magic or otherwise. Lumping these together is... unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, let's leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Carry on then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 04-30-2019, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T09:55:37-07:00","id":1308946,"title":"","content":"Reproduction and gender may not directly relate, but they are certainly topics that share some links. I'm not sure why discussing them together is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:36:12-07:00","id":1308965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308946#post1308946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reproduction and gender may not directly relate, but they are certainly topics that share some links. I'm not sure why discussing them together is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, indirectly, because expectations for gender in long-term relationships tend to include fertility.<br /> So that's going to be brought up in most relationships. Some people are fine with that, some are not.<br /> it's also a notable topic because trans people are the exception, and that's only ever going to change following medical improvements that develop ways to perfectly transition and/or to re-wire the brain into a cis configuration. Needless to say neither will happen anytime soon, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> Discussing this is only as bad as the people want it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T11:31:20-07:00","id":1308979,"title":"","content":"Also it's not bad per say, but it can complicated discussions a lot more than is good for the conversation.<br /> <br /> To get away from Exalted (but not far from the topic at hand):<br /> <br /> If I was a reproductive scientist and a couple came to me to help them have children, their gender identities don't impact the nature of the procedures needed to make that happen. What matters are the gametes the couple can provide, and if surrogacy is preferred/necessary.<br /> <br /> There is a huge and important intersectional discussion around all of that (esp. regarding personal financial resources, and society resources, and how those biases who can get what services)... but it's not helpful to a discussion of what science can do for a couple trying to reproduce on a basic level of &quot;here's what we can do.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T22:48:37-07:00","id":1309111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308965#post1308965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do, indirectly, because expectations for gender in long-term relationships tend to include fertility.<br /> So that's going to be brought up in most relationships. Some people are fine with that, some are not.<br /> it's also a notable topic because trans people are the exception, and that's only ever going to change following medical improvements that develop ways to perfectly transition and/or to re-wire the brain into a cis configuration. Needless to say neither will happen anytime soon, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> Discussing this is only as bad as the people want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say, can you tell me how cis people's brains differ from trans people of the same gender? I'd love to hear your theory on how actually all this scientific research on the matter is incorrect and that trans men have the same brains as cis women or trans women have the same brains as cis men. Or is the &quot;political zeitgeist&quot; too stifling for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","user":"SunAndSpring","date":". 05-01-2019, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","name":"SunAndSpring","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12698_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T23:18:57-07:00","id":1309114,"title":"","content":"I think you're misreading that.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the point is that trans people require significant medical intervention to transition their bodies into the closest they can get to what they want, and there's only two ways to resolve that: sufficient medical technology to make physical assignment changes a trivial matter (distant future if ever of technology), or sufficient technology to literally erase trans identity by rewiring trans brains to the cis brains on the opposite side of the gender spectrum (also far off, and incredibly horribly immoral).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T23:25:51-07:00","id":1309117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309114#post1309114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're misreading that.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the point is that trans people require significant medical intervention to transition their bodies into the closest they can get to what they want, and there's only two ways to resolve that: sufficient medical technology to make physical assignment changes a trivial matter (distant future if ever of technology), or sufficient technology to literally erase trans identity by rewiring trans brains to the cis brains on the opposite side of the gender spectrum (also far off, and incredibly horribly immoral).</div> </div> </div> </div>No I'm pretty sure he's just some right-wing dipshit. That shit whining about the political zeitgeist just being too mean to intellectuals such as he is a red flag.<br /> <br /> Like lol, I can search his fucking post history on Reddit, it's nothing but bitching about taxes and unions and LGBT people, why should I give him the benefit of the doubt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","user":"SunAndSpring","date":". 05-01-2019, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","name":"SunAndSpring","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12698_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T02:03:06-07:00","id":1309141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1308965#post1308965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do, indirectly, because expectations for gender in long-term relationships tend to include fertility.<br /> So that's going to be brought up in most relationships. Some people are fine with that, some are not.<br /> it's also a notable topic because trans people are the exception, and that's only ever going to change following medical improvements that develop ways to perfectly transition and/or to re-wire the brain into a cis configuration. Needless to say neither will happen anytime soon, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> Discussing this is only as bad as the people want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I need to re-wire my brain into a cis-configuration? Oh wow!<br /> <br /> Anyway, see, transpeople are not the exception, far from it! We are only a tiny minority. Lots of people do not have children, some because they can not, for a variety of reasons, some because they don't want to. And there is indeed the expectation of having children, especially for women where in the mind of many being a woman and being a mother is about the same thing.<br /> <br /> I know my girlfriend was sick and tired of being posed the question of when she was planning to have kids. I have friends who wanted them but couldn't. Very few of them, whether voluntarily or not, did not at times feel their identity as women was under pressure due to expectations and societal pressure. And yes, I'm talking cis-women (equipped with cis-brains!).<br /> <br /> Now, is discussion about fixing reproduction with ritual magic in the Exalted setting somehow not politically correct? Of course not! But it is something that affects everyone, cis, trans, men, women and everything in between. Doing so with as in the thread title 'transgender' inevitable leads to unfortunate implications, such as implying the capacity and willingness to have children is needed to be a man or women. We already got some gems, like, transition without reproduction only getting you part of the way, and that wonderfully charming concept of the cis-brain!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T05:39:38-07:00","id":1309150,"title":"","content":"I NEVER said you need anything, and made ZERO judgment. Stop assuming whatever you want from my text before you even consider having that conversation.<br /> In fact, the overall tone of my statement was that in an ideal world treating gender dysphoria however you want shouldn't be more inconvenient than, say, removing your gallbladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 05-01-2019, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T05:53:51-07:00","id":1309154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunAndSpring</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309111#post1309111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say, can you tell me how cis people's brains differ from trans people of the same gender? I'd love to hear your theory on how actually all this scientific research on the matter is incorrect and that trans men have the same brains as cis women or trans women have the same brains as cis men. Or is the &quot;political zeitgeist&quot; too stifling for you?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\"> pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.3109/09540261.2015.1113163\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full...1.2015.1113163</a><br /> <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/cercor/article/28/5/1582/3064956\" target=\"_blank\">https://academic.oup.com/cercor/arti...5/1582/3064956</a><br /> <br /> The few recorded attempts to treat it as something exclusively developmental showed, at best, failure.<br /> There are evolutionary atavisms that could explain this.<br /> <br /> Our understanding of how transgenderism and dysphoria happens is limited, because of course it is, but given there <i>are</i> measurable neural differences between sexes and correlations with transgender people, it would be disingenuous to assume these things do not exist or to ignore them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T07:06:27-07:00","id":1309157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunAndSpring</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309117#post1309117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I'm pretty sure he's just some right-wing dipshit. That shit whining about the political zeitgeist just being too mean to intellectuals such as he is a red flag.<br /> <br /> Like lol, I can search his fucking post history on Reddit, it's nothing but bitching about taxes and unions and LGBT people, why should I give him the benefit of the doubt</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>If you believe a poster's activity elsewhere is evidence that they are posting in bad faith you bring that to me, In the meantime this is a personal attack. </b></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T07:32:10-07:00","id":1309166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309154#post1309154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\"> pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21334362 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.3109/09540261.2015.1113163\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full...1.2015.1113163</a><br /> <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/cercor/article/28/5/1582/3064956\" target=\"_blank\">https://academic.oup.com/cercor/arti...5/1582/3064956</a><br /> <br /> The few recorded attempts to treat it as something exclusively developmental showed, at best, failure.<br /> There are evolutionary atavisms that could explain this.<br /> <br /> Our understanding of how transgenderism and dysphoria happens is limited, because of course it is, but given there <i>are</i> measurable neural differences between sexes and correlations with transgender people, it would be disingenuous to assume these things do not exist or to ignore them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are quite right, our understanding is limited, especially as in regards to the causes of dysphoria or a gender identity not matching your biological sex (however you wish to define that these days). As with most of these more complex issues there is likely an interplay between different causes at play.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, the more modern scientific work is beginning to abandon the concept of dimorphism. These measurable differences, if they even exist, are purely statistical, as in, not saying anything about the individual, and the variation within the group is definitely much, much larger than whatever might exist between the groups.<br /> <br /> As said, that these statistical differences even exist is contested. There are studies, such as Daphna Joel's, and many other but that is the one that I came across first, that have found no evidence for two distinct types of brain, but mainly many different combinations of characteristics, i.e. heterogeneous populations. Furthermore, these differences are often due to external factors. For example, it can be shown that a \u201ccharacteristically male\u201d density of dendritic spines or branches of a nerve cell can be changed to the \u201cfemale\u201d form simply by the application of a mild external stress.<br /> <br /> In short, indications currently are that speaking of a 'male' vs 'female' brain is unproductive. This applies to many more fields than neurology, by the way.<br /> <br /> Now, that there are differences between the two sexes and how it all maps to gender identity I will not argue. If there weren't I would never have experienced dysphoria, that much is obvious, but we don't know the specifics. All we know now is that gender identity is a spectrum, as are the physical differences between men and woman in general. Trying to find something somewhere that when you 'have it' or 'don't have it' makes you a 'real' man or woman is a fool's game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 05-01-2019, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T07:47:35-07:00","id":1309171,"title":"","content":"This particular post was just a response to SunAndSpring's request. I originally touched on that technicality because we were talking about limitations of modern medicine and how they relate...<br /> <br /> Other than that we agree on how the topic is complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T19:46:28-07:00","id":1309359,"title":"","content":"So as I understand it the question at hand is can a Sorcerous working of Terrestrial level give not just look alike genitalia. Now honestly I can think of several ways a terrestrial level working could do this The most obvious is to break down a female body that had a functional reproductive system and transfer that to another. As organ and tissue transplantation is something medical science has today.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think there is something else to consider it's not the science of Trans and Homosexuality its Culture.<br /> Firstly let's look at the realm. The realm values women over men. To the point that men are are faced with a very real glass ceiling that prevents them from rising to ranks in military service and similar fields that are half that of a woman. Only a female officer can command a whole dragon of troops. Moreover the realm closely monitors bloodlines and house rankings. A male is not a shameful child to give birth to but the realm is matrilineal so the daughter inherits not the son. The male marries into his wife's family. Which brings us to Dowery. The fact is having a male child in the realm means you will give up power and wealth to another family. That isn't something the matriarch of the family can allow. Now if she can turn all her Son's into Daughters. then she can acquire power and wealth over giving it away. I think the use of any magic to switch one's sex in the realm would be restricted and may even require any dynasts to give up their status in their houses and become as lost eggs, and be signed off on by the house matriarch. Because the last thing the isle needs is the probable facing china today where there are several orders of magnitude more males than females (only reversed) where there are several orders of magnitude more females than males.<br /> <br /> Let's look elsewhere, In some other cultures one may discover a culture that doesn't tolerate homosexuality, but does transgender status. Meaning that in another light you may have people who aren't trans, pretending to be trans because it's easy to say that than admit the truth. They aren't truly trans so they never elect to undergo a transformation. More over cultures where gender determines occupation like the one that Prince Diamond comes from also may have many people who are not truly trans &quot;taking the grey&quot; just to do what they want to do with their lives. If they ever moved into a different culture one that doesn't have such strict rules, or just doesn't care, then guess what. They will immediately take off their grey and not care unless they go home to visit their parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly Creation isn't the kind of world where they are going to spend a lot of time thinking about anything that doesn't lead to the survival and thriving of the species (humanity). Ergo again no one gives a shit about who's gay, or who's a lesbian, or if those two families over there the wives are sharing a bed, and the husbands are too loud when they are doing it; producing offspring only as often as legally required to keep their marriages and thus their farms. The only people who care are tax collectors, magistrates, keepers of law, and keepers of records. That's it for the common person. The Dragon blooded have other pressures other cultural things going on.<br /> <br /> Hell in earlier editions Big Red herself created a culture where being Bisexual, and Promiscuous is fashionable. Meaning you had dragon blooded men and woman who were homosexual or strait pretending to be bisexual. This is actually one thing very close to how the real world worked. Anything a monarch was or did is going to be mirrored by their subjects because that is how it was back in the earlier days. So yeah...culture. Think about how it applies. When you do you start to see...creation isn't some inclusive utopia it's another world just as shitty as ours, just as oppressive as ours, just in different ways and reasons because they have magic, which could solve some problems we have but would create more new problems as a side effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T23:23:22-07:00","id":1309579,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty clear that the reason for that limitation is narrative; it's made difficult to <i>perfectly</i> resolve the problems people face with magic because that leads to more interesting stories where, for instance, people cut bargains or take risks or go on adventures in order to obtain their desires. (Of course, individual people might reasonably differ on whether being unable to reproduce is an &quot;imperfect&quot; solution, especially if they didn't intend to reproduce to begin with. But it's at least going to bother some people, which leads them to want more powerful magic in order to get what they want, which leads to interesting stories.)<br /> <br /> I suspect that when answering questions like the one mentioned in this thread, the devs think about &quot;what makes a good story&quot; before &quot;what fits into the setting's metaphysics.&quot; But this is also, probably, something you should decide at your table based on the stories your players want to tell.<br /> <br /> Another factor is probably an unwillingness to make it too easy to wave a magic wand to resolve problems that are harder to deal with in the real world - hence the fairly blunt &quot;TCS solves it exactly as well as modern medicine can.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-03-2019, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T02:06:25-07:00","id":1309598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309579#post1309579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty clear that the reason for that limitation is narrative; it's made difficult to <i>perfectly</i> resolve the problems people face with magic because that leads to more interesting stories where, for instance, people cut bargains or take risks or go on adventures in order to obtain their desires. (Of course, individual people might reasonably differ on whether being unable to reproduce is an &quot;imperfect&quot; solution, especially if they didn't intend to reproduce to begin with. But it's at least going to bother some people, which leads them to want more powerful magic in order to get what they want, which leads to interesting stories.)<br /> <br /> I suspect that when answering questions like the one mentioned in this thread, the devs think about &quot;what makes a good story&quot; before &quot;what fits into the setting's metaphysics.&quot; But this is also, probably, something you should decide at your table based on the stories your players want to tell.<br /> <br /> Another factor is probably an unwillingness to make it too easy to wave a magic wand to resolve problems that are harder to deal with in the real world - hence the fairly blunt &quot;TCS solves it exactly as well as modern medicine can.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically we nerf magic because of the real world that's not the system Exalted was intended for. The current devs didn't even make the system in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T02:30:40-07:00","id":1309601,"title":"","content":"Well, no. Terrestrial sorcery can absolutely allow someone to reproduce regardless of biology. They're called neomah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T02:33:38-07:00","id":1309602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309601#post1309601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no. Terrestrial sorcery can absolutely allow someone to reproduce regardless of biology. They're called neomah.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not the same and also comes with issues. What if the sorcerer was paid to fuck with you or the neomah was pretending to be bound and wasn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T03:36:17-07:00","id":1309611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309598#post1309598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically we nerf magic because of the real world that's not the system Exalted was intended for. The current devs didn't even make the system in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it nerfing Sorcery? Workings are a massive expansion of what Sorcery - which was already powerful without it - can do. And again, we're not even talking about &quot;can or can't&quot; do something, but how difficult it is for a character to pull off. This sort of hyperbolic response isn't helping anything.<br /> <br /> I think a bigger take away is the one of the problems with 3e is that the core book added either entirely brand new things (Workings) or extremely new takes on old things (crafting) that aren't explained well for the devs intentions (and yes, we've changed devs, but the current team was there for the development of the core book). We get very vague guides in the book, we go to the devs for help, and they give us guidelines that - however decent and useful they might be - end up making things less clear with some of the examples. That's basically the whole primary thrust of this thread. It's what lead to things like making a quiver of ten arrows is ten Basic projects instead of one Major project, but making a multiple course banquet is a single Major project because one is batching and one isn't... even if it makes it really hard to say where the line on batching actually is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309602#post1309602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really not the same and also comes with issues. What if the sorcerer was paid to fuck with you or the neomah was pretending to be bound and wasn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the goal is to pop out a baby that's the product of two individuals... the neomah is probably a better choice from a practical stand point; even if having children is not something done strictly based on that sort of thinking.<br /> <br /> And... what if the sorcerer you go to to change your body to conform to your gender got paid to fuck with you? Or are we forcing every trans DB to learn Sorcery if they want to do this (which would be kinda messed up even if it was ruled a Terrerstial Working)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T03:39:12-07:00","id":1309612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309598#post1309598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The current devs didn't even make the system in place.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if memory serves, the sorcery chapter was Robert Vance's baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:42:22-07:00","id":1309616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309579#post1309579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty clear that the reason for that limitation is narrative; it's made difficult to <i>perfectly</i> resolve the problems people face with magic because that leads to more interesting stories where, for instance, people cut bargains or take risks or go on adventures in order to obtain their desires. (Of course, individual people might reasonably differ on whether being unable to reproduce is an &quot;imperfect&quot; solution, especially if they didn't intend to reproduce to begin with. But it's at least going to bother some people, which leads them to want more powerful magic in order to get what they want, which leads to interesting stories.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That limitation is particularly interesting to make celestial and solar sorcerers something akin to a devil. Here you are in this unfair world where even the sorcerous might of the Realm cannot help you. The few sorcerers even capable of doing that will not, for you are but a dynast of low station, and those guys answer directly to the Throne.<br /> <br /> But fret not, my poor, unfortunate soul. Travel away from the blessed isle. Reach my fortress of living ice deep within the wasting tundra. You will but owe me a favor <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:54:41-07:00","id":1309620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309612#post1309612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if memory serves, the sorcery chapter was Robert Vance's baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so, yeah. Though presumably with input from the devs at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T05:47:54-07:00","id":1309625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309611#post1309611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... what if the sorcerer you go to to change your body to conform to your gender got paid to fuck with you? Or are we forcing every trans DB to learn Sorcery if they want to do this (which would be kinda messed up even if it was ruled a Terrerstial Working)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the sorcerer botches. That could be pretty unpleasant.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T06:53:49-07:00","id":1309633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309625#post1309625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the sorcerer botches. That could be pretty unpleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, it could be unpleasant when it all goes as planned. Sorcery is meant to be weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T07:10:58-07:00","id":1309637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309633#post1309633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, it could be unpleasant when it all goes as planned. Sorcery is meant to be weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my old games had a sorcerer and a wood-king signify the pact they'd made by each trading the other one of his eyes. Any elemental who met the sorcerer's gaze knew he carried that wood-king's authority with him.<br /> <br /> But he still had to take his eye out, and replace it with one made of wood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T08:31:27-07:00","id":1309656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309611#post1309611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or are we forcing every trans DB to learn Sorcery if they want to do this (which would be kinda messed up even if it was ruled a Terrerstial Working)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that sorcery is far from the only means of transitioning in Creation.<br /> <br /> There's mundane methods - the tea brewed from herbs and the sweat of pregnant mares that the Sisterhood of the Night Ride uses, and I'm sure there's some culture or cultures who're clever enough to do HRT with alchemy. <br /> <br /> As far as magic goes, in addition to sorcery, thaumaturgy and spirit's blessings can provide transition. A Solar or Lunar physician could provide damn good medical transition - presumably a Dynastic Dragon-Blood wouldn't want to deal with them, but maybe there's Exigent with suitable skills they could strike a deal with. There's also magical places of power, like a demesne where a font of clear-flowing water blesses those who drink from its source with a body that matches their gender euphoriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:21:11-07:00","id":1309675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309656#post1309656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also magical places of power, like a demesne where a font of clear-flowing water blesses those who drink from its source with a body that matches their gender euphoriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though hopefully you don't get it mixed up with the spring that turns you into a panda.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:28:38-07:00","id":1309678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309675#post1309675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though hopefully you don't get it mixed up with the spring that turns you into a panda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow. <br /> <br /> I now remember oglaf <br /> <br /> 'Fountain of Blonde-haired bimbo'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:42:53-07:00","id":1309685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309678#post1309678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow.<br /> <br /> I now remember oglaf</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referencing <i>Ranma Nibun-no-Ichi</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:34:31-07:00","id":1309693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309685#post1309685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referencing <i>Ranma Nibun-no-Ichi</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my.<br /> <br /> ...... shows the train of thought, doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:37:23-07:00","id":1309694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309611#post1309611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it nerfing Sorcery? Workings are a massive expansion of what Sorcery - which was already powerful without it - can do. And again, we're not even talking about &amp;quot;can or can't&amp;quot; do something, but how difficult it is for a character to pull off. This sort of hyperbolic response isn't helping anything.<br /> <br /> I think a bigger take away is the one of the problems with 3e is that the core book added either entirely brand new things (Workings) or extremely new takes on old things (crafting) that aren't explained well for the devs intentions (and yes, we've changed devs, but the current team was there for the development of the core book). We get very vague guides in the book, we go to the devs for help, and they give us guidelines that - however decent and useful they might be - end up making things less clear with some of the examples. That's basically the whole primary thrust of this thread. It's what lead to things like making a quiver of ten arrows is ten Basic projects instead of one Major project, but making a multiple course banquet is a single Major project because one is batching and one isn't... even if it makes it really hard to say where the line on batching actually is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If the goal is to pop out a baby that's the product of two individuals... the neomah is probably a better choice from a practical stand point; even if having children is not something done strictly based on that sort of thinking.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A person who wants wings can get wings. These work. They might be a little weird to use but these wings fly. They do what they need to and have bith an in story amd in game benefit. A person who changed their gender. Didn't actually change their gender. They just did it cosmetically and superficially. When you can prodoce mutations that are true and create new beings. You are basically saying that for no reason, you are nerfing this ability. The rules as written do no at all support this ruling and it doesn't help the game at all to support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:42:53-07:00","id":1309696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309694#post1309694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person who changed their gender. Didn't actually change their gender. They just did it cosmetically and superficially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender is not your capacity to make babies - it's what you identify as. We've been over this. A person doesn't need to undergo surgery or magic or HRT, they just have to identify as the gender other than the one they were designated as at birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-03-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:46:48-07:00","id":1309697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309696#post1309696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender is not your capacity to make babies. We've been over this. A person doesn't need to undergo surgery or HRT to be transgender, they just have to identify as the gender other than the one they were designated as at birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises hand*<br /> <br /> This may be potentially insensitive. I know little about trans issues. Apologies. <br /> <br /> Ok, these guys identify as the gender other htan the one they were designated as at birth. Designated, using, well, their physical forms. <br /> <br /> So the current hullaballoo seems to be about... transforming one's body from male to female? Or female to male? And the sorcerous workings not being good enough for it, for some reason? <br /> <br /> One of the differences between two genders, is one can bear children, and the other cannot. <br /> <br /> In this case, does not being unable to conceive serve as an indication that the transformation is incomplete?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:50:46-07:00","id":1309702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309696#post1309696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender is not your capacity to make babies - it's what you identify as. We've been over this. A person doesn't need to undergo surgery or magic or HRT, they just have to identify as the gender other than the one they were designated as at birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a lot of transpeople, being able to reproduce is something they still want to. You're saying these people are essentially wrong in this desire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T11:55:33-07:00","id":1309705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309702#post1309702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To a lot of transpeople, being able to reproduce is something they still want to. You're saying these people are essentially wrong in this desire?</div> </div> </div> </div>No he's saying that linking gender to being able to reproduce is inherently insensitive and wrong.<br /> <br /> There are thousands of cis people who cannot have children for one reason or another. Men who have had vasectomies are still men. Women who have had hysterectomies are still women. Sterile men or women are still men and women.<br /> <br /> Saying that a woman isn't a woman because she cannot bear children is fucking insulting.<br /> <br /> Saying that a man isn't a man because he cannot father children is fucking insulting.<br /> <br /> Both of these things are what you're saying EVERY TIME you say that the transition isn't 'good enough' or isn't 'complete' without the ability to have children. I would really appreciate if you chose a different argument because it's goddamn disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 05-03-2019, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T12:03:45-07:00","id":1309711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309702#post1309702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a lot of transpeople, being able to reproduce is something they still want to. You're saying these people are essentially wrong in this desire?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <b>I'm</b> saying that the desire to reproduce is not the same as the realization that someone identifies as a different gender than the one a doctor slapped on their birth certificate. You can want one, or the other, or both, or neither.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have no idea where you seem to have got this notion, as no one seems to be arguing that trans people shouldn't be allowed to reproduce.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Well, okay, <i>some</i> people are arguing that. But not here. It's generally taking place in some pretty gross websites.)<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309697#post1309697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, these guys identify as the gender other htan the one they were designated as at birth. Designated, using, well, their physical forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't necessarily accurate. You'd be surprised at the number of people born intersex. Deciding the gender of someone by how their genitals look at birth is a pretty flawed method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309697#post1309697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the current hullaballoo seems to be about... transforming one's body from male to female? Or female to male? And the sorcerous workings not being good enough for it, for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hullaballoo is about whether or not it's reasonable for a gender-reaffirming sorcerous working to <i>also</i> give the person the capacity to produce children. Which, as we've said, is not a prerequisite of maleness or femaleness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309697#post1309697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the differences between two genders, is one can bear children, and the other cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. My girlfriend cannot bear children, and is not trans. Nor does a trans man have to have his uterus surgically removed just because he identifies as male.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298457-sidebar-on-transgender-dynasts?p=1309697#post1309697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, does not being unable to conceive serve as an indication that the transformation is incomplete?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-03-2019, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions"